WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.600
Always, always, the mahloket is a detail of the Torah, never and one of the akkadim.

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:15.600
Let me explain to you, it's a very, very, very important, and also intellectually, it's

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:16.600
one of the great principles.

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:17.600
The thing is the following.

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:21.760
There's been a mahloket in the Gemara, I don't know, it goes into the thousands of

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:23.559
mahloket controversies.

00:00:23.559 --> 00:00:29.639
And not only in the Gemara, in postal music, you know, the geonim, they go into the mahloket,

00:00:29.639 --> 00:00:35.639
but the postal music, you know, in the Middle Ages, mahloket, opinions, one says this, the

00:00:35.639 --> 00:00:36.639
other says that.

00:00:36.639 --> 00:00:44.439
Now, very, let me ask you from a philosophical point of view, yes, Suleiha, can anybody close

00:00:44.439 --> 00:00:52.759
the door please, because there is a draft, all right, suppose, I don't know, there is

00:00:52.759 --> 00:01:00.919
a pasuk, all right, ze, livi, anvehu, elohi, aviv, baromeh, whatever it is, so I give an

00:01:00.919 --> 00:01:13.279
expression A, and you give an expression B, all right, how can we resolve, how could,

00:01:13.279 --> 00:01:17.480
what we're going to use to resolve this mahloket, in other words, what criteria we're going

00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:18.480
to use.

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:19.480
Does that answer my question?

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:27.720
Now, suppose I want to say, all right, I'm going to use criteria X, listen to this, is

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:33.080
this X written in the Torah, if it's written in the Torah, then let's go to X, how could

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:37.440
it be a controversy, you understand, how, you're going to say, well, no, I'm going to

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:42.800
solve it through logic, all right, I'm going to solve it through logic, yes, I'm going

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:48.160
to argue my point through logic, you argue your point through logic, so then it means

00:01:48.199 --> 00:01:53.360
that the Torah ultimately is conditioned by human logic, so how could it be, something

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:59.120
that comes from God is conditioned by human logic, the truth is, that's a very important

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:04.599
principle of the Geonim, and of Harambam, etc., so Hakam David, Rabbi David Nieto here,

00:02:04.599 --> 00:02:11.520
that's what he says, there can never be a mahloket on something which isn't in the Torah,

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:17.000
there is no mahloket, there is no controversy, because if there would be a controversy, there

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:22.960
would be no possible way to resolve it, the controversies, that's what the point of Harambam

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:31.199
makes it very strongly, the Geonim, the controversies are always undetails, which are not explicit

00:02:31.199 --> 00:02:36.320
in the Torah, and because they are not explicit in the Torah, then I could say, it should

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:46.320
be this way, let me give you an example, Sepharadim Ashkenazim, how we put on the tefillin of

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:54.440
the hand, according to the Ashkenazim, you have to stand up, according to the Sepharadim,

00:02:54.440 --> 00:03:01.320
you sit down, now if you look into the Gemara, into the whole Gemara, you are not going to

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:07.479
find that says, tefillin shelyad, you must sit down, because if they would say you must

00:03:07.479 --> 00:03:12.800
sit down, then how could the Ashkenazim stand up, conversely, in no place you are going

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:18.880
to find the Gemara that says, tefillin shelyad, you have to stand up, because if we look at

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:24.839
the Sepharadim, they are going to say this, therefore, this is a question of, alright,

00:03:24.839 --> 00:03:28.119
since you are going to add two tefillin more, to add tefillin shelyad, tefillin sherosh,

00:03:28.119 --> 00:03:35.360
how you do it, alright, so one says, my opinion is A, the other says, my opinion is B, now,

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:40.679
here comes a very important thing, people do not know this, if this mahloket is only

00:03:40.679 --> 00:03:46.679
on something, on a detail, which is not in the Torah, it means the following, that if

00:03:46.679 --> 00:03:53.800
I put it, instead of sitting down, standing up, or instead of standing up, I sit down,

00:03:53.800 --> 00:04:00.080
it is alright, because there never could be a controversy, that is the point that is very

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:05.679
very important, there never was, and there never should be, a controversy on something

00:04:05.679 --> 00:04:11.160
which is really in the Torah, what is in the Torah, that is called in Hebrew, a hakkar,

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:17.279
that is a fundament, because it is written in the Torah, there cannot be a controversy,

00:04:17.279 --> 00:04:20.799
all the controversies that you have, that is the point of Harambam, that is the point

00:04:20.799 --> 00:04:27.600
of Geonim, that is the point of Rabbi David Neto here, all those controversies must pertain

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:35.239
to a detail, which in itself, is not ultimately relevant, and it says that you do it the other

00:04:35.239 --> 00:04:38.720
way, it is also good, do you understand what I am trying to say, so therefore, all those

00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:44.679
who want to interpret mahloket, do it any way you want to, but do not think that if

00:04:44.679 --> 00:04:49.000
you do it the other way, it is the end of the world, do you understand what I am trying

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:53.679
to say, this is very very important, because again, if you are going to say that under

00:04:53.679 --> 00:04:58.519
Torah itself, there is a controversy, you are saying, you are postulating two things

00:04:58.519 --> 00:05:04.640
which are unacceptable, number one, is that the tradition was not good, because here is

00:05:04.640 --> 00:05:09.720
something which is in the Torah, one of the 613 commandments, and somehow, the Hakamim,

00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:16.720
they didn't transmit it good, so the transmission was not alright, so that is one point, we

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:22.519
cannot accept such a thing, because ultimately we have to say, oh, our tradition is faithful,

00:05:22.519 --> 00:05:26.920
and second, if there is a controversy, you are not going to resolve it by applying criteria

00:05:26.920 --> 00:05:34.720
A, B, C, D, which is not in the Torah, that means that there is something about the Torah,

00:05:34.720 --> 00:05:38.880
that conditions the Torah, again, we cannot accept it, this is the point that is going

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:43.320
to be developed here, all the mahlokot that there are, there are many controversies in

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:53.119
the Gemara, and in post-Gemara, they always pertain to details, not to Ikkar, clear this

00:05:53.119 --> 00:05:56.119
point? Very important, no?

00:05:56.119 --> 00:06:02.119
I mean, but we do find sometimes mahlokot that pertain to, let's say something about

00:06:02.119 --> 00:06:06.119
Shabbat, you know, and then you say, well, according to us, if we do it that way, we

00:06:06.119 --> 00:06:08.119
are not, we are making Ahavon instead of Shabbat.

00:06:08.119 --> 00:06:12.119
Yeah, but I would say making Ahavon, but not in the Torah. Cannot be.

00:06:12.119 --> 00:06:13.119
Oh, I see what you are saying.

00:06:13.119 --> 00:06:17.119
They cannot be, they could not be in the Torah that there is a controversy, that is the point

00:06:17.119 --> 00:06:22.119
of Arambam, as a matter of fact, I am going to tell you how Arambam works. If there is

00:06:22.119 --> 00:06:29.119
a controversy on something, that is a proof for Arambam that it is not in the Torah. Because

00:06:29.119 --> 00:06:35.119
it is impossible to either stipulate that the tradition of the Torah faltered, or that

00:06:35.119 --> 00:06:40.119
there is a criterion outside the Torah by which we could resolve this mahlokot. You

00:06:40.119 --> 00:06:41.119
understand?

00:06:41.119 --> 00:06:49.119
So, according to Arambam, that is impossible to have a controversy on something which is

00:06:49.119 --> 00:06:54.119
in the Torah. If there is a controversy, prove that this is not in the Torah.

00:06:54.119 --> 00:06:59.119
It is a seyah, the interpretation, whatever you want to call it, it is not in the Torah.

00:06:59.119 --> 00:07:02.119
There cannot be a controversy on something which is in the Torah. Now, of course, today

00:07:02.119 --> 00:07:06.119
we have people that they don't know, and they will, for instance, they tell you to wear

00:07:06.119 --> 00:07:11.119
long sleeves for a girl is in the Torah. The truth is that it is not in the Torah, even

00:07:11.119 --> 00:07:14.119
according to their opinion, because if you open the head of the Torah, you know, no place

00:07:14.119 --> 00:07:21.119
you are going to find about wearing this. So they use the word Torah in a non-exact,

00:07:21.119 --> 00:07:28.119
precise manner. But the truth is, there cannot be a controversy on anything which is really

00:07:28.119 --> 00:07:33.119
in the Torah. Alright? This is the point.

00:07:34.119 --> 00:07:43.119
Now, the left column, obviously, and 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 lines from the bottom.

00:07:53.119 --> 00:08:01.119
These are akarim, they are principles. Nobody, maybe only one person may understand this

00:08:01.119 --> 00:08:08.119
Arabic, in Arabic called usul din. These are the akarim, it comes, you know, it was

00:08:09.119 --> 00:08:14.119
Spanish speaking, but the same idea comes, the notion of akarim, usul din. And then they

00:08:14.119 --> 00:08:21.119
have in Arabic, the Jews, they use this word, they have furu' din. Furu' means branches

00:08:21.119 --> 00:08:29.119
of. The details, literally it means, usul means roots, and furu' means branches. And

00:08:29.119 --> 00:08:33.119
the other are, if there is a mahlukat, as in the language of Hambam, this is only

00:08:33.119 --> 00:08:39.119
be furu' din, not be usul din. Alright? So I am just, you know, telling you this thing.

00:08:39.119 --> 00:08:40.119
Alright.

00:08:47.119 --> 00:08:49.119
This is not only among the tanayim.

00:08:50.119 --> 00:09:00.119
Even the demorayim, less, but they also had kabbalah which came directly to them. Alright?

00:09:02.119 --> 00:09:08.119
And there was no mahlukat among the demorayim on the laws which are really in the Torah.

00:09:08.119 --> 00:09:14.119
No mahlukat. That's for Hambam, this is a Syriac one-armed principle. Alright?

00:09:19.119 --> 00:09:24.119
I will give you an example, things that come from there. We are going to go into the laws

00:09:24.119 --> 00:09:26.119
of glad kosher, non-glad kosher. Alright?

00:09:28.119 --> 00:09:33.119
There are, Hambam and Hammamim wrote many statements, sher raba, made by raba. Raba

00:09:33.119 --> 00:09:41.119
was around the year 3050 of the common era. 3050, no, maybe it should be less, more. I

00:09:41.119 --> 00:09:47.119
would say around the year 380 of the common era. And now he's going to make statements.

00:09:47.119 --> 00:09:51.119
They are not based upon a baraitah, it's not that he's quoting a baraitah, or a mishnah,

00:09:51.119 --> 00:09:56.119
or he's quoting another rabbi. But it's simply, he's quoting you the tradition as probably

00:09:56.119 --> 00:10:02.119
was the living shohet tradition of the slaughtering houses at his time and they are in it.

00:10:03.119 --> 00:10:05.119
And nobody ever disagreed with him.

00:10:07.119 --> 00:10:11.119
And this is unquoting, Rabbi David Nieto says.

00:10:11.119 --> 00:10:19.119
Re'ah shiafshah mikshatah terefah. As I said to you, Jewish medicine is different than

00:10:19.119 --> 00:10:23.119
Greek medicine. And now we understand the wisdom of Jewish medicine. Greek medicine,

00:10:23.119 --> 00:10:29.119
it centered everything on the heart. The heart was for them the key of good health. For the

00:10:29.119 --> 00:10:35.119
Jew, Jewish medicine was different. They saw always in the lung the key to understand the

00:10:35.119 --> 00:10:42.119
health of that thing. If your lungs are healthy, then the heart is healthy, etc., etc.

00:10:44.119 --> 00:10:50.119
Interesting, that's true. Now, your heart could be healthy and your other things could be

00:10:50.119 --> 00:10:57.119
also sick because the heart is the strongest of all the muscles. So for it to be healthy,

00:10:57.119 --> 00:11:02.119
it doesn't mean that all the rest of the body is healthy. But there are, I don't know, maybe

00:11:02.119 --> 00:11:08.119
it's weaker. I don't know medicine. But I read once an article that this is supposed to be the

00:11:08.119 --> 00:11:15.119
key for health is the Re'ah. Now it says like this, Re'ah shiafshah mikshatah, that some

00:11:15.119 --> 00:11:22.119
of it is dry. It means it does not fill with air because already it's dry. Even a little

00:11:22.119 --> 00:11:31.119
bit of it. Terefah. And when you go to x-ray from the lungs, one of the things immediately

00:11:32.119 --> 00:11:37.119
they say is we want to see whether the Re'ah is shiafshah or not. Because if it's shiafshah,

00:11:37.119 --> 00:11:42.119
that is a small bar minan that the person may be in trouble. So shiafshah means when

00:11:42.119 --> 00:11:47.119
it already is dry. Dry by dry means there is no moisture and therefore it does not expand

00:11:47.119 --> 00:11:52.119
and contract. And expand means that air does not enter there. Once the air enters like

00:11:52.119 --> 00:11:58.119
this, the animal is teref, which means it could die within 12 months. In the case of

00:11:58.119 --> 00:12:05.119
us, Baruch Hashem, we have modern medicine, etc. But I just wanted to know. So this is

00:12:05.119 --> 00:12:11.119
a statement, mey baravah. It brings no proof. It just says it and it's accepted by everybody.

00:12:11.119 --> 00:12:16.119
Again, an example of a tradition from the time of the Moraim that comes to them not

00:12:16.119 --> 00:12:24.119
via the Mishnah or the Baraitah. Re'ah maravah. En leh tarteh oneh, dezerichan lehadadeh,

00:12:24.119 --> 00:12:40.119
sheh loke sidran, terefah. Now the lung has partitions. Partitions. It's not one thing.

00:12:40.119 --> 00:12:46.119
It's made of actually five things. And the things are called onot. Each one of those

00:12:46.119 --> 00:12:53.119
compartments. If they are tied one with the other, sheh loke sidran, not in the proper

00:12:53.119 --> 00:12:58.119
order. The one that's supposed to be on top is on the bottom. And the one at the bottom

00:12:58.119 --> 00:13:05.119
is on the top. Yes? The thing, the animal is teref. Although it has all the lungs, it's

00:13:05.119 --> 00:13:13.119
complete, but it's not sheh loke sidran. There's no good. Re'ah maravah. Do you understand

00:13:13.119 --> 00:13:21.119
what I'm saying? Onah is the thing that fills with air. It means there's five compartments

00:13:21.119 --> 00:13:29.119
in the lung. Yes? Of the animal or our things. The five things. Yes? And there's the upper

00:13:29.119 --> 00:13:35.119
part. It's called lobes. It's called lobes? Lobes. Two on the left, three on the right.

00:13:35.119 --> 00:13:40.119
Yes. Now if you have the onah, it's called in English lobes. If the lobes are not in

00:13:40.119 --> 00:13:47.119
the order, the one that's supposed to be down is up. Or up is down. The animal is teref.

00:13:48.119 --> 00:13:51.119
A defect. It's a defect. A genetic defect.

00:14:00.119 --> 00:14:11.119
The law is the following. In the re'ah, there are two skins. It has two skins. If only one

00:14:11.119 --> 00:14:23.119
skin has a hole, whether the upper one or the lower one, it's not teref. It's only teref

00:14:23.119 --> 00:14:32.119
when they have a nekeb, a hole that goes through both skins. Now, this is law number one. I

00:14:32.119 --> 00:14:41.119
want you to understand. So if the nekeb peers through both skins, then and then alone, it's

00:14:41.119 --> 00:14:54.119
teref. Now, sometimes the animal has a hole in the re'ah, and then a bu'ah grows on top

00:14:54.119 --> 00:15:05.119
of it. A bu'ah is like a skin. It's a very thin skin. Like a cyst. Just like if you get

00:15:05.119 --> 00:15:13.119
burned. If you get burned. Like a scar. You know, like sometimes you get burned or you

00:15:13.119 --> 00:15:21.119
get something like white in your skin, full of water, you know. Not a blister. A blister.

00:15:21.119 --> 00:15:29.119
Like full of water, you know. So that is called, that is a bu'ah. Listen to this. Now, you have,

00:15:29.119 --> 00:15:35.119
now you're a shohet, you open and you look into the re'ah, you look into the lungs. And you see

00:15:35.119 --> 00:15:45.119
if there is a bu'ah, one single bu'ah, yes, then you could be bodek and find out the following.

00:15:45.119 --> 00:15:53.119
So a good bodek could tell you whether this is covering a hole, in which case the animal

00:15:53.119 --> 00:15:59.119
is teref and you're not permitted to eat it. Or sometimes it grows like this. It grows, a cyst

00:15:59.119 --> 00:16:07.119
grows like that. Without a hole. So now, you have the re'ah and you're the shohet. And there is

00:16:07.119 --> 00:16:19.119
a bu'ah. Bu'ah means one single thing like this. Alright? So, if it's one alone, then you could

00:16:19.119 --> 00:16:24.119
bodek. You make bedekah. I'll tell you in a second how you make bedekah. Alright? You make bedekah

00:16:24.119 --> 00:16:35.119
and you see whether actually there is a hole, in which case it's teref, or there is no hole.

00:16:35.119 --> 00:16:43.119
In that case, it's kasher. How you make bedekah? Very simple. You take, that's the way Harambam

00:16:43.119 --> 00:16:48.119
says it, that's the way the Temanim say it, we don't do it this way. But just let me tell you first

00:16:48.119 --> 00:16:53.119
the way the Harambam and the Temanim do it, which I think is the best. But we don't do it this way.

00:16:53.119 --> 00:17:01.119
They take maim poshrim, lukewarm water, you put the re'ah there, and then you blow it.

00:17:01.119 --> 00:17:10.119
If there's bubbles coming out, that means that there's a hole. You see? If there are no bubbles

00:17:10.119 --> 00:17:16.119
coming out, then there is kasherah. That's the way Harambam says to make bedekah.

00:17:16.119 --> 00:17:17.119
We make it, what?

00:17:17.119 --> 00:17:20.119
If it is a hole and it's covering it up, how is it going to come out?

00:17:20.119 --> 00:17:26.119
Oh, it will come out through, I'm sorry, then you would see this bu'ah standing up.

00:17:26.119 --> 00:17:34.119
Because it looks like a bubble. And also bubbles will come out from the skin.

00:17:34.119 --> 00:17:41.119
The skin apparently does not close things hermetically.

00:17:41.119 --> 00:17:46.119
We don't do it this way. The Sepharadim and the Ashkenazim also don't do it this way.

00:17:46.119 --> 00:17:50.119
How they do it, Sepharadim and Ashkenazim, they do it by blowing it without the hot water,

00:17:50.119 --> 00:17:56.119
without the lukewarm water. Why? Because they're afraid that the lukewarm water, maybe it's going to,

00:17:56.119 --> 00:18:05.119
there's some dirt from the animal, you know, blood and so on, and will be sotem the naked.

00:18:05.119 --> 00:18:12.119
You see? No, close it, close it. So therefore we do it, I did it and I saw it many times,

00:18:12.119 --> 00:18:18.119
although I'm not an expert, I'm not a bodek, yes? But I saw it many times and I was taught how to do it.

00:18:18.119 --> 00:18:23.119
We blow it and then somebody else looks into it and see whether the thing is standing or not.

00:18:23.119 --> 00:18:31.119
If it's standing, then obviously it has a hole. And if it is not standing, that means that there is no hole.

00:18:31.119 --> 00:18:37.119
Or if there is a hole, maybe on one skin, but not on both skins. You see? And that is kosher.

00:18:37.119 --> 00:18:49.119
However, if there are two buahot, not one buahot, two buahot, the law is we don't make medikah, we declare taref.

00:18:49.119 --> 00:18:55.119
You see? And Aram Bam says why? He says because maybe the hole is in between them.

00:18:55.119 --> 00:19:04.119
And then you cannot, it's not that each one is covering a different hole,

00:19:04.119 --> 00:19:10.119
but between both of them, between two of them, there is one single hole and sometimes it is,

00:19:10.119 --> 00:19:14.119
and therefore by blowing it this way you cannot make, it cannot tell.

00:19:14.119 --> 00:19:20.119
Now, no, no, two, one, no, no, one, no, if there are two, together, together.

00:19:20.119 --> 00:19:23.119
And also how do you know whether they are called together or they are separate?

00:19:23.119 --> 00:19:29.119
Very simple. You blow one of them. If the other one stands, it means that they are together.

00:19:30.119 --> 00:19:37.119
You see? In this case, we don't care. We don't make the medikah of the two.

00:19:37.119 --> 00:19:43.119
If they are together, this is where the glad kosher, non-glad kosher comes about.

00:19:43.119 --> 00:19:52.119
The glad kosher means that if you see anything in the lung, immediately, two buahot, one buahot, you don't make medikah.

00:19:52.119 --> 00:19:56.119
Immediately you declare it unkosher, you give it to the unkosher butcher.

00:19:56.119 --> 00:20:00.119
But according to the non-glad, you are bodek.

00:20:00.119 --> 00:20:02.119
And I told you the history of it. It is very simple.

00:20:02.119 --> 00:20:08.119
In Ashkenazi communities, they were limited in the amount of animals that they were given by the goyim,

00:20:08.119 --> 00:20:10.119
even in modern times.

00:20:10.119 --> 00:20:15.119
And therefore they had to, for example, suppose you are a village, they give you five cows.

00:20:15.119 --> 00:20:20.119
So if you are going to say that two cows are taref, then two-thirds of the meat product is this.

00:20:20.119 --> 00:20:24.119
So they were much careful, and before they declared taref, they would make all kinds of medikot,

00:20:24.119 --> 00:20:29.119
and we trust, of course, that a shohet is a trustworthy, should be a trustworthy individual,

00:20:29.119 --> 00:20:31.119
and therefore if he tells you it is kosher, it should be kosher.

00:20:31.119 --> 00:20:34.119
It is not going to be just like that.

00:20:34.119 --> 00:20:41.119
I was told that in the past, maybe 20 or 30 years ago, there was no concept of kosher.

00:20:41.119 --> 00:20:44.119
Absolutely correct. Absolutely correct.

00:20:44.119 --> 00:20:47.119
I want to tell you how it came.

00:20:47.119 --> 00:20:53.119
It came, incidentally, a teacher of my teacher, Rabbi Isaac Abu Al-A'afi, was involved in this thing.

00:20:53.119 --> 00:20:57.119
Many years ago, the Turks, they only recognized the Sephardim.

00:20:57.119 --> 00:20:59.119
They didn't recognize the Ashkenazim.

00:20:59.119 --> 00:21:06.119
Simply because we were citizens of Turkish territory, and the Ashkenazim, they were not.

00:21:06.119 --> 00:21:15.119
So they wanted to have shehita, separate shehita, the Ashkenazim, in Israel.

00:21:15.119 --> 00:21:19.119
For economic reasons, they wanted to sell to the people,

00:21:19.119 --> 00:21:22.119
and listen, it's an income, and that's the ethical law.

00:21:22.119 --> 00:21:25.119
They wanted to have the income for them, so rather than this.

00:21:25.119 --> 00:21:37.119
So the question was, I'm sorry, at one time, the Turkish government gave to one Ashkenazic group permission to make shehita.

00:21:37.119 --> 00:21:40.119
So then they came the Hasidim, or I don't know from where or not,

00:21:40.119 --> 00:21:45.119
and they apparently didn't get along with the other group, and they wanted to open their own shehita.

00:21:45.119 --> 00:21:50.119
So now the Turkish says, we are Ashkenazim, we are Sephardim, what do you want?

00:21:50.119 --> 00:21:51.119
Another one.

00:21:51.119 --> 00:21:56.119
So they say, oh, we are Ashkenazim, but we want to make the laws not like this,

00:21:56.119 --> 00:22:03.119
they make with the ri'ad, we want to make it halak, you know, glad like the Sephardim.

00:22:03.119 --> 00:22:07.119
So, and therefore we want to have separate thing.

00:22:07.119 --> 00:22:10.119
So the teacher of my teacher, Rabbi Isaac Abu Al-A'afi, was one of the ones,

00:22:10.119 --> 00:22:13.119
he was in Tiberias at the time, he intervened on behalf of the Ashkenazim,

00:22:13.119 --> 00:22:17.119
to get them, let them have a permit from the Turkish government,

00:22:17.119 --> 00:22:22.119
probably because maybe he had tools, I don't know exactly, the bureaucracy.

00:22:22.119 --> 00:22:31.119
And they were able to get the permit, and therefore now they justify the shehita as being glad.

00:22:31.119 --> 00:22:37.119
Now in America, when I came to America, there was no such a concept of glad kosher.

00:22:38.119 --> 00:22:40.119
There was none. Why?

00:22:40.119 --> 00:22:44.119
Because the Ashkenazim themselves, the Ashkenazimia, they were in charge of shehita,

00:22:44.119 --> 00:22:47.119
they were not from the Hasidim, you see.

00:22:47.119 --> 00:22:53.119
And they came, I don't know, from Warsaw, from Minsk or Pinsk or one of the large cities,

00:22:53.119 --> 00:22:56.119
and those cities, they had ration, they rationed the cows,

00:22:56.119 --> 00:22:59.119
and they would make shehita, not glad.

00:22:59.119 --> 00:23:02.119
I ate from it. Why?

00:23:02.119 --> 00:23:04.119
Because the law is as simple as this.

00:23:04.119 --> 00:23:07.119
Yes, we Sephardim, we eat halak.

00:23:07.119 --> 00:23:09.119
That's the malang, they say.

00:23:09.119 --> 00:23:11.119
Not one bu'a?

00:23:11.119 --> 00:23:14.119
Not one bu'a, if there's a bu'a, no, if there's bu'a, one bu'a,

00:23:14.119 --> 00:23:19.119
no, even one bu'a, they don't, they don't, they don't destroy it.

00:23:19.119 --> 00:23:23.119
And I told you the reason why, because we used to be slaughtering the same slaughterhouse as the Muslims.

00:23:23.119 --> 00:23:30.119
Why should we even, it's more waste time to be bodek, this bu'a,

00:23:30.119 --> 00:23:33.119
than to give it to the goy, and you take another one, and you shehet.

00:23:33.119 --> 00:23:35.119
What's the problem? It's much easier.

00:23:35.119 --> 00:23:38.119
So, by law, that was the custom.

00:23:38.119 --> 00:23:41.119
But, here comes the point, the very important point.

00:23:41.119 --> 00:23:45.119
There was a question asked to the shehita, Haim David of Sephardi Zulay,

00:23:45.119 --> 00:23:46.119
one of the hachamim.

00:23:46.119 --> 00:23:51.119
He says, you are a Sephardi shaliyah, from Eretz Yisrael.

00:23:51.119 --> 00:23:54.119
So the shehita used to go travel all over the world.

00:23:54.119 --> 00:23:58.119
Now, you are in a place in which the shehita is only a shekinazit.

00:23:58.119 --> 00:24:01.119
Alright? Non-glad.

00:24:01.119 --> 00:24:04.119
You Sephardi, you follow my lad.

00:24:04.119 --> 00:24:06.119
Can you eat from that shehita?

00:24:06.119 --> 00:24:08.119
He says, of course you can. Why?

00:24:08.119 --> 00:24:11.119
That's also my policy. Why?

00:24:11.119 --> 00:24:16.119
Because there's, we have a kelal, a rule.

00:24:16.119 --> 00:24:19.119
Rob behemot kesherot hain.

00:24:19.119 --> 00:24:22.119
Teneffa always is an anomaly.

00:24:22.119 --> 00:24:25.119
And we always, in the laws of kashrut, we follow the rob.

00:24:25.119 --> 00:24:31.119
So therefore, we always assume that this behemot had no problem.

00:24:31.119 --> 00:24:33.119
Why? Because of the kelal.

00:24:33.119 --> 00:24:35.119
Rob behemot kesherot hain.

00:24:35.119 --> 00:24:36.119
Alright?

00:24:36.119 --> 00:24:41.119
The only time that you should abstain, or may want to abstain,

00:24:41.119 --> 00:24:48.119
is if you know for sure that this behemot had bua.

00:24:48.119 --> 00:24:51.119
And they made betika, that according to maran is not good,

00:24:51.119 --> 00:24:54.119
and according to that, then and then along, you should abstain.

00:24:54.119 --> 00:24:56.119
So now, here I eat and go to a restaurant.

00:24:56.119 --> 00:24:58.119
I go to Louis Segal.

00:24:58.119 --> 00:25:00.119
Yes, now Louis Segal also is halak.

00:25:00.119 --> 00:25:02.119
But when I used to come to Louis Segal, it was not halak.

00:25:02.119 --> 00:25:04.119
I'm eating a steak.

00:25:04.119 --> 00:25:07.119
My assumption is, rob behemot kesherot hain.

00:25:07.119 --> 00:25:09.119
And that's the end of it.

00:25:09.119 --> 00:25:10.119
Alright?

00:25:10.119 --> 00:25:12.119
So, that's my policy till today.

00:25:12.119 --> 00:25:15.119
And I also believe that, of course,

00:25:15.119 --> 00:25:17.119
each one, we should have traditions and so on,

00:25:17.119 --> 00:25:21.119
but we should not use the tradition to make mahlukot between the Jews.

00:25:21.119 --> 00:25:22.119
No!

00:25:22.119 --> 00:25:25.119
Now, suppose I'm married to Ashkenazi woman,

00:25:25.119 --> 00:25:28.119
so therefore I'm not going to be able to eat on my mother-in-law.

00:25:28.119 --> 00:25:30.119
No, that's ridiculous. That's stupid.

00:25:30.119 --> 00:25:31.119
You know?

00:25:31.119 --> 00:25:32.119
Or vice versa.

00:25:32.119 --> 00:25:33.119
I'm into this type of things and say,

00:25:33.119 --> 00:25:36.119
ah, they use the Jewish law to make mahlukot,

00:25:36.119 --> 00:25:40.119
controversies between communities.

00:25:40.119 --> 00:25:42.119
No, we should not make.

00:25:42.119 --> 00:25:45.119
And the truth is, as I say, rob behemot kesherot hain.

00:25:45.119 --> 00:25:47.119
That's the pesak of the hida.

00:25:47.119 --> 00:25:48.119
And I follow it.

00:25:48.119 --> 00:25:49.119
Yes?

00:25:50.119 --> 00:25:51.119
Oh, yes.

00:25:57.119 --> 00:25:58.119
Yes.

00:25:58.119 --> 00:26:02.119
The glad people and the non-glad people, they check their lungs.

00:26:02.119 --> 00:26:06.119
The only difference is that the non-glad,

00:26:06.119 --> 00:26:08.119
if they see some anomaly,

00:26:08.119 --> 00:26:10.119
they would try to maybe,

00:26:10.119 --> 00:26:12.119
to say maybe we could kosher it.

00:26:12.119 --> 00:26:13.119
You know?

00:26:13.119 --> 00:26:16.119
By checking, by blowing this well and making...

00:26:20.119 --> 00:26:21.119
My opinion?

00:26:21.119 --> 00:26:22.119
You don't.

00:26:22.119 --> 00:26:25.119
Because we assume that rob behemot kesherot.

00:26:25.119 --> 00:26:26.119
Now, if you want to eat...

00:26:26.119 --> 00:26:27.119
I eat glad.

00:26:29.119 --> 00:26:30.119
If you...

00:26:30.119 --> 00:26:31.119
But I'm going to say...

00:26:31.119 --> 00:26:34.119
The truth is more complex than this.

00:26:36.119 --> 00:26:38.119
The way Maran wants it,

00:26:38.119 --> 00:26:40.119
even the glad kosher don't have it.

00:26:40.119 --> 00:26:43.119
Because Maran, if you see one single buah,

00:26:43.119 --> 00:26:45.119
according to Maran, you should get out.

00:26:45.119 --> 00:26:47.119
Even the glad kosher,

00:26:47.119 --> 00:26:48.119
what the glad kosher is,

00:26:48.119 --> 00:26:49.119
they don't do it for two buahot,

00:26:49.119 --> 00:26:50.119
like Hia says.

00:26:50.119 --> 00:26:51.119
You know?

00:26:51.119 --> 00:26:53.119
But for one buahot, there would be megavitika.

00:26:53.119 --> 00:26:55.119
So, let us not fool ourselves.

00:26:55.119 --> 00:26:57.119
Exactly, exactly like Maran,

00:26:58.119 --> 00:26:59.119
they don't do it.

00:26:59.119 --> 00:27:02.119
Even, there is one place that my son, A.B.,

00:27:02.119 --> 00:27:03.119
used to buy,

00:27:03.119 --> 00:27:05.119
it's called glad Maran.

00:27:05.119 --> 00:27:06.119
It's called in America.

00:27:06.119 --> 00:27:07.119
And he used to buy it from one place,

00:27:07.119 --> 00:27:08.119
I don't know where.

00:27:08.119 --> 00:27:09.119
And he...

00:27:09.119 --> 00:27:10.119
I went there for a few times,

00:27:10.119 --> 00:27:11.119
I ate it, horrible meat.

00:27:11.119 --> 00:27:12.119
But, that's not the point.

00:27:12.119 --> 00:27:13.119
Not the point.

00:27:13.119 --> 00:27:15.119
The point is, fine.

00:27:15.119 --> 00:27:16.119
But there is a difference

00:27:16.119 --> 00:27:18.119
between Sepharadim and the knife.

00:27:18.119 --> 00:27:22.119
We make different sharpen.

00:27:22.119 --> 00:27:24.119
So, they are not going to make the sharpen

00:27:24.119 --> 00:27:25.119
like the Sepharadim.

00:27:25.119 --> 00:27:28.119
So, what ultimately you are going to say,

00:27:28.119 --> 00:27:29.119
I am going to eat it.

00:27:29.119 --> 00:27:30.119
I, not like Maran,

00:27:30.119 --> 00:27:31.119
in the cushion of the knife.

00:27:31.119 --> 00:27:32.119
So, you are going to tell me,

00:27:32.119 --> 00:27:34.119
robemot kisherotem.

00:27:34.119 --> 00:27:35.119
That's fine.

00:27:35.119 --> 00:27:36.119
So, therefore, let's go all the way,

00:27:36.119 --> 00:27:37.119
robemot kisherotem.

00:27:37.119 --> 00:27:38.119
So, that's...

00:27:38.119 --> 00:27:41.119
So, I, again,

00:27:41.119 --> 00:27:43.119
these are peripherals,

00:27:43.119 --> 00:27:47.119
and I believe they should not be elaborated.

00:27:47.119 --> 00:27:49.119
And I believe that sometimes

00:27:49.119 --> 00:27:52.119
this could turn into discord

00:27:52.119 --> 00:27:53.119
between communities.

00:27:53.119 --> 00:27:54.119
And I believe that

00:27:54.119 --> 00:27:58.119
tabiah hachavim marvim shalom ba'olam.

00:27:58.119 --> 00:27:59.119
We should not...

00:27:59.119 --> 00:28:00.119
So, this...

00:28:00.119 --> 00:28:01.119
And that's why,

00:28:01.119 --> 00:28:02.119
with all due respect,

00:28:02.119 --> 00:28:03.119
I totally, absolutely,

00:28:03.119 --> 00:28:05.119
categorically disagree with ourself

00:28:05.119 --> 00:28:07.119
that says that you cannot go to sefer torah

00:28:07.119 --> 00:28:08.119
of Ashkenazim.

00:28:08.119 --> 00:28:09.119
Ashkenazim cannot go to sefer torah

00:28:09.119 --> 00:28:10.119
of the Sepharadim,

00:28:10.119 --> 00:28:11.119
which I think is crazy.

00:28:11.119 --> 00:28:12.119
And also about the tefillin,

00:28:12.119 --> 00:28:15.119
that the tefillin of the Sepharadim is different.

00:28:15.119 --> 00:28:17.119
Selechamike vodo.

00:28:17.119 --> 00:28:19.119
That's right.

00:28:19.119 --> 00:28:20.119
Yeah.

00:28:20.119 --> 00:28:21.119
You should not go.

00:28:21.119 --> 00:28:22.119
And vice versa.

00:28:22.119 --> 00:28:23.119
Because the sefer torah is different.

00:28:23.119 --> 00:28:24.119
The sheen is different.

00:28:24.119 --> 00:28:25.119
You know.

00:28:25.119 --> 00:28:27.119
And also the tefillin

00:28:27.119 --> 00:28:28.119
says if you have a Sepharadim,

00:28:28.119 --> 00:28:29.119
you should not go.

00:28:29.119 --> 00:28:30.119
My opinion,

00:28:30.119 --> 00:28:32.119
and that was the opinion of

00:28:32.119 --> 00:28:33.119
Bishak Abul Afia,

00:28:33.119 --> 00:28:34.119
my teacher's teacher,

00:28:34.119 --> 00:28:35.119
you should wear

00:28:35.119 --> 00:28:36.119
the kateh la.

00:28:36.119 --> 00:28:37.119
I could wear

00:28:37.119 --> 00:28:38.119
a tefillin,

00:28:38.119 --> 00:28:39.119
the Ashkenazim,

00:28:39.119 --> 00:28:40.119
the Ashkenazim,

00:28:40.119 --> 00:28:41.119
Sepharadim,

00:28:41.119 --> 00:28:42.119
torah,

00:28:42.119 --> 00:28:43.119
I absolutely

00:28:43.119 --> 00:28:44.119
not want

00:28:44.119 --> 00:28:45.119
whatsoever

00:28:45.119 --> 00:28:46.119
to

00:28:46.119 --> 00:28:47.119
intercommunal

00:28:47.119 --> 00:28:48.119
thing.

00:28:48.119 --> 00:28:49.119
And by the way,

00:28:49.119 --> 00:28:50.119
as I tell you,

00:28:50.119 --> 00:28:51.119
I mean,

00:28:51.119 --> 00:28:52.119
it is silly.

00:28:52.119 --> 00:28:53.119
And also,

00:28:53.119 --> 00:28:54.119
when I go to

00:28:54.119 --> 00:28:55.119
Ashkenazic

00:28:55.119 --> 00:28:56.119
minyan,

00:28:56.119 --> 00:28:57.119
if I could pray

00:28:57.119 --> 00:28:58.119
like them,

00:28:58.119 --> 00:28:59.119
I pray

00:28:59.119 --> 00:29:00.119
exactly like them.

00:29:00.119 --> 00:29:01.119
I don't think

00:29:01.119 --> 00:29:02.119
there is

00:29:02.119 --> 00:29:03.119
no superior

00:29:03.119 --> 00:29:04.119
between Baruch

00:29:04.119 --> 00:29:05.119
and Boruch.

00:29:05.119 --> 00:29:06.119
Boruch

00:29:06.119 --> 00:29:07.119
understands Hebrew,

00:29:07.119 --> 00:29:08.119
all pronunciations

00:29:08.119 --> 00:29:09.119
of Hebrew.

00:29:09.119 --> 00:29:10.119
Boruch

00:29:10.119 --> 00:29:11.119
for me

00:29:11.119 --> 00:29:12.119
is the same.

00:29:12.119 --> 00:29:13.119
Same thing,

00:29:13.119 --> 00:29:14.119
same tefillin,

00:29:14.119 --> 00:29:15.119
same this.

00:29:15.119 --> 00:29:16.119
Now,

00:29:16.119 --> 00:29:17.119
in my life,

00:29:17.119 --> 00:29:18.119
I say Baruch

00:29:18.119 --> 00:29:19.119
because I was

00:29:19.119 --> 00:29:20.119
trained Baruch.

00:29:20.119 --> 00:29:21.119
But if I were to be a child

00:29:21.119 --> 00:29:22.119
and I was to be in

00:29:22.119 --> 00:29:23.119
an Ashkenazic community

00:29:23.119 --> 00:29:24.119
and I was to say

00:29:24.119 --> 00:29:25.119
Boruch,

00:29:25.119 --> 00:29:26.119
I would say Boruch.

00:29:26.119 --> 00:29:27.119
And I cannot be,

00:29:27.119 --> 00:29:28.119
I have to be totally stupid

00:29:28.119 --> 00:29:29.119
to say,

00:29:29.119 --> 00:29:30.119
ah,

00:29:30.119 --> 00:29:31.119
God said,

00:29:31.119 --> 00:29:32.119
no,

00:29:32.119 --> 00:29:33.119
one minute.

00:29:33.119 --> 00:29:34.119
He said,

00:29:34.119 --> 00:29:35.119
Boruch.

00:29:35.119 --> 00:29:36.119
I'm not going to accept.

00:29:36.119 --> 00:29:37.119
That's ridiculous.

00:29:37.119 --> 00:29:38.119
The same thing,

00:29:38.119 --> 00:29:39.119
we are one people

00:29:39.119 --> 00:29:40.119
which are the result

00:29:40.119 --> 00:29:41.119
of Galut

00:29:41.119 --> 00:29:42.119
and nothing more than that.

00:29:42.119 --> 00:29:43.119
And nobody should think

00:29:43.119 --> 00:29:44.119
my prayer

00:29:44.119 --> 00:29:45.119
is better than

00:29:45.119 --> 00:29:46.119
their prayer

00:29:46.119 --> 00:29:47.119
or vice versa.

00:29:47.119 --> 00:29:48.119
Our prayers are all

00:29:48.119 --> 00:29:49.119
tekubal berason,

00:29:49.119 --> 00:29:50.119
every single community.

00:29:50.119 --> 00:29:51.119
Sephardim,

00:29:51.119 --> 00:29:52.119
Ashkenazim,

00:29:52.119 --> 00:29:53.119
Italkim,

00:29:53.119 --> 00:29:54.119
Temanim,

00:29:54.119 --> 00:29:55.119
Persians,

00:29:55.119 --> 00:29:56.119
the same thing.

00:29:56.119 --> 00:29:57.119
That's my thing.

00:29:57.119 --> 00:29:58.119
We should not be silly.

00:29:58.119 --> 00:29:59.119
All right.

00:29:59.119 --> 00:30:00.119
Yeah?

00:30:00.119 --> 00:30:01.119
Yeah.

00:30:01.119 --> 00:30:02.119
Yes,

00:30:02.119 --> 00:30:03.119
but it's based

00:30:03.119 --> 00:30:04.119
on the Gemara.

00:30:04.119 --> 00:30:05.119
The Gemara is

00:30:05.119 --> 00:30:06.119
the tropics

00:30:06.119 --> 00:30:07.119
and the mountains.

00:30:07.119 --> 00:30:08.119
So we

00:30:09.119 --> 00:30:10.119
question of statistics

00:30:10.119 --> 00:30:11.119
and by

00:30:11.119 --> 00:30:12.119
in shahitan,

00:30:12.119 --> 00:30:13.119
you follow statistics.

00:30:13.119 --> 00:30:14.119
How do you know

00:30:14.119 --> 00:30:15.119
that there is no

00:30:15.119 --> 00:30:16.119
tumor in the brain?

00:30:16.119 --> 00:30:17.119
Rub him

00:30:17.119 --> 00:30:18.119
or kishirot him.

00:30:18.119 --> 00:30:19.119
How do you know

00:30:19.119 --> 00:30:20.119
there is no tumor

00:30:20.119 --> 00:30:21.119
in the liver?

00:30:21.119 --> 00:30:22.119
Rub him

00:30:22.119 --> 00:30:23.119
or kishirot him.

00:30:23.119 --> 00:30:24.119
So the same thing

00:30:24.119 --> 00:30:25.119
you say on the reha,

00:30:25.119 --> 00:30:26.119
on the lung.

00:30:26.119 --> 00:30:27.119
Don't,

00:30:27.119 --> 00:30:28.119
you know,

00:30:28.119 --> 00:30:29.119
like this,

00:30:29.119 --> 00:30:30.119
you know,

00:30:30.119 --> 00:30:31.119
those are all problems,

00:30:31.119 --> 00:30:32.119
you know,

00:30:32.119 --> 00:30:33.119
and so on.

00:30:33.119 --> 00:30:34.119
And if the shohed

00:30:34.119 --> 00:30:35.119
made a mistake,

00:30:35.119 --> 00:30:36.119
it's his mistake,

00:30:36.119 --> 00:30:37.119
it's not my mistake.

00:30:37.119 --> 00:30:38.119
You know,

00:30:38.119 --> 00:30:39.119
if the shohed made a mistake

00:30:39.119 --> 00:30:40.119
and he's fooling me,

00:30:40.119 --> 00:30:41.119
I mean,

00:30:41.119 --> 00:30:42.119
I'm not responsible to God.

00:30:42.119 --> 00:30:43.119
You know,

00:30:43.119 --> 00:30:44.119
I eat shahitan.

00:30:44.119 --> 00:30:45.119
This guy,

00:30:45.119 --> 00:30:46.119
he told me shohed,

00:30:46.119 --> 00:30:47.119
and look,

00:30:47.119 --> 00:30:48.119
that's it,

00:30:48.119 --> 00:30:49.119
you know.

00:30:49.119 --> 00:30:50.119
That is not the goal.

00:30:50.119 --> 00:30:51.119
God is not

00:30:51.119 --> 00:30:52.119
looking to harm us.

00:30:52.119 --> 00:30:53.119
You know,

00:30:53.119 --> 00:30:54.119
we do as much as we can.

00:30:54.119 --> 00:30:55.119
That's all.

00:30:55.119 --> 00:30:56.119
You know,

00:30:56.119 --> 00:30:57.119
we don't have to be

00:30:57.119 --> 00:30:58.119
hysterical about it.

00:30:58.119 --> 00:30:59.119
That's my position

00:30:59.119 --> 00:31:00.119
and I'm very strong

00:31:00.119 --> 00:31:01.119
about this.

00:31:01.119 --> 00:31:02.119
All right?

00:31:02.119 --> 00:31:03.119
Yeah,

00:31:03.119 --> 00:31:04.119
this is ridiculous.

00:31:04.119 --> 00:31:05.119
It's absolutely ridiculous.

00:31:05.119 --> 00:31:06.119
You know,

00:31:06.119 --> 00:31:07.119
this,

00:31:07.119 --> 00:31:08.119
you know,

00:31:08.119 --> 00:31:09.119
this,

00:31:09.119 --> 00:31:10.119
you know,

00:31:10.119 --> 00:31:11.119
I,

00:31:11.119 --> 00:31:12.119
I,

00:31:12.119 --> 00:31:13.119
it is,

00:31:13.119 --> 00:31:14.119
you know,

00:31:14.119 --> 00:31:15.119
God says,

00:31:15.119 --> 00:31:16.119
tamim tiyeh

00:31:16.119 --> 00:31:17.119
ima Adonai Elohecha.

00:31:17.119 --> 00:31:18.119
You should be

00:31:18.119 --> 00:31:19.119
simple with God.

00:31:19.119 --> 00:31:20.119
Don't be

00:31:20.119 --> 00:31:21.119
too complicated with God.

00:31:21.119 --> 00:31:22.119
Tamim tiyeh

00:31:22.119 --> 00:31:23.119
ima Adonai Elohecha.

00:31:23.119 --> 00:31:24.119
You know,

00:31:24.119 --> 00:31:25.119
Hakam Oyakov

00:31:25.119 --> 00:31:26.119
in Cassini,

00:31:26.119 --> 00:31:27.119
and Hakam

00:31:27.119 --> 00:31:28.119
Matlub Abadi,

00:31:28.119 --> 00:31:29.119
they bought

00:31:29.119 --> 00:31:30.119
meat from the regular butcher.

00:31:30.119 --> 00:31:31.119
They didn't buy

00:31:31.119 --> 00:31:32.119
glad meat,

00:31:32.119 --> 00:31:33.119
you know,

00:31:33.119 --> 00:31:34.119
and so on.

00:31:34.119 --> 00:31:35.119
Anyhow,

00:31:35.119 --> 00:31:36.119
today I'm buying

00:31:36.119 --> 00:31:37.119
glad.

00:31:37.119 --> 00:31:38.119
I'm going to say

00:31:38.119 --> 00:31:39.119
because my wife

00:31:39.119 --> 00:31:40.119
buys the glad

00:31:40.119 --> 00:31:41.119
because,

00:31:41.119 --> 00:31:42.119
I don't know,

00:31:42.119 --> 00:31:43.119
she is the religious one.

00:31:43.119 --> 00:31:44.119
All right?

00:31:44.119 --> 00:31:45.119
That's the point.

00:31:45.119 --> 00:31:46.119
Anyhow,

00:31:46.119 --> 00:31:47.119
now,

00:31:47.119 --> 00:31:48.119
v'amalava

00:31:48.119 --> 00:31:49.119
hamesh

00:31:49.119 --> 00:31:50.119
oneh

00:31:50.119 --> 00:31:51.119
itlah

00:31:51.119 --> 00:31:52.119
l're'ah.

00:31:52.119 --> 00:31:53.119
The re'ah

00:31:53.119 --> 00:31:54.119
has five

00:31:54.119 --> 00:31:55.119
lobes,

00:31:55.119 --> 00:31:56.119
we say the word is?

00:31:56.119 --> 00:31:57.119
Lobes.

00:31:57.119 --> 00:31:58.119
Five lobes.

00:31:58.119 --> 00:31:59.119
Apah

00:31:59.119 --> 00:32:00.119
has

00:32:00.119 --> 00:32:01.119
five lobes.

00:32:01.119 --> 00:32:02.119
Apah

00:32:02.119 --> 00:32:03.119
has

00:32:03.119 --> 00:32:04.119
five lobes.

00:32:04.119 --> 00:32:05.119
Apah

00:32:05.119 --> 00:32:06.119
ke'lah g'abrah

00:32:06.119 --> 00:32:07.119
and they,

00:32:07.119 --> 00:32:08.119
when you

00:32:08.119 --> 00:32:09.119
slaughter,

00:32:09.119 --> 00:32:10.119
they're looking at you.

00:32:10.119 --> 00:32:11.119
The face,

00:32:11.119 --> 00:32:12.119
the

00:32:12.119 --> 00:32:13.119
the

00:32:13.119 --> 00:32:14.119
the smallest,

00:32:14.119 --> 00:32:15.119
the

00:32:15.119 --> 00:32:16.119
the angle

00:32:16.119 --> 00:32:17.119
is towards you,

00:32:17.119 --> 00:32:18.119
and the

00:32:18.119 --> 00:32:19.119
white part

00:32:19.119 --> 00:32:20.119
is towards the back of the animal.

00:32:20.119 --> 00:32:21.119
All right?

00:32:21.119 --> 00:32:22.119
When you open this way.

00:32:22.119 --> 00:32:23.119
Yes.

00:32:23.119 --> 00:32:24.119
All right?

00:32:24.119 --> 00:32:25.119
So,

00:32:25.119 --> 00:32:26.119
it says,

00:32:26.119 --> 00:32:27.119
now,

00:32:27.119 --> 00:32:28.119
telatah mi'minah

00:32:28.119 --> 00:32:29.119
there are three lobes

00:32:29.119 --> 00:32:30.119
on the right side,

00:32:30.119 --> 00:32:32.119
utreh mi'semalah

00:32:32.119 --> 00:32:33.119
and two lobes

00:32:33.119 --> 00:32:34.119
on the

00:32:34.119 --> 00:32:35.119
left.

00:32:35.119 --> 00:32:37.119
Yihasir.

00:32:37.119 --> 00:32:39.119
If any lobe is missing.

00:32:39.119 --> 00:32:41.119
Yiyatir.

00:32:41.119 --> 00:32:43.119
If there is an extra lobe.

00:32:43.119 --> 00:32:45.119
Yihalif.

00:32:45.119 --> 00:32:47.119
If you have three on the left and two on the right.

00:32:47.119 --> 00:32:49.119
Terefah.

00:32:49.119 --> 00:32:51.119
And all those traditions,

00:32:51.119 --> 00:32:53.119
the word traditions,

00:32:53.119 --> 00:32:54.119
reported

00:32:54.119 --> 00:32:55.119
by an emora

00:32:55.119 --> 00:32:56.119
about a year,

00:32:56.119 --> 00:32:57.119
I say,

00:32:57.119 --> 00:32:58.119
more or less,

00:32:58.119 --> 00:32:59.119
370

00:32:59.119 --> 00:33:00.119
of the coming era,

00:33:00.119 --> 00:33:01.119
doesn't mention in the name of

00:33:01.119 --> 00:33:02.119
aparaitah or amishnah

00:33:02.119 --> 00:33:03.119
and they were accepted

00:33:03.119 --> 00:33:04.119
by all Jews.

00:33:04.119 --> 00:33:05.119
So, therefore,

00:33:05.119 --> 00:33:06.119
this is another example

00:33:06.119 --> 00:33:07.119
of ekarim.

00:33:07.119 --> 00:33:08.119
Yes?

00:33:08.119 --> 00:33:09.119
Of principles

00:33:09.119 --> 00:33:10.119
that they were part of our tradition

00:33:10.119 --> 00:33:11.119
and we continue to transmit

00:33:11.119 --> 00:33:12.119
one generation

00:33:12.119 --> 00:33:13.119
after the other.

00:33:13.119 --> 00:33:15.119
And nobody ever disagrees with them.

00:33:15.119 --> 00:33:16.119
If there would be

00:33:16.119 --> 00:33:17.119
a disagreement,

00:33:17.119 --> 00:33:18.119
Harambam would call it

00:33:18.119 --> 00:33:20.119
a non-ekar.

00:33:20.119 --> 00:33:21.119
Because no Jew,

00:33:21.119 --> 00:33:22.119
no rabbi,

00:33:22.119 --> 00:33:23.119
would disagree

00:33:23.119 --> 00:33:24.119
on an ekar,

00:33:24.119 --> 00:33:25.119
something which is in the Torah.

00:33:25.119 --> 00:33:27.119
V'chem bechol ad-dinim

00:33:27.119 --> 00:33:29.119
bem be-dineh ma'ononot

00:33:29.119 --> 00:33:30.119
bem be-dineh nefashot

00:33:30.119 --> 00:33:31.119
the word

00:33:31.119 --> 00:33:32.119
da'karim

00:33:32.119 --> 00:33:33.119
and that da'karim

00:33:33.119 --> 00:33:34.119
there is no machloket.

00:33:34.119 --> 00:33:35.119
If you find a machloket,

00:33:35.119 --> 00:33:37.119
that is not an ekar.

00:33:37.119 --> 00:33:40.119
Simple as that.

00:33:40.119 --> 00:33:42.119
Hosef v'habe'ot

00:33:42.119 --> 00:33:43.119
masha'allah chair.

00:33:43.119 --> 00:33:44.119
Why don't you bring me

00:33:44.119 --> 00:33:45.119
another example

00:33:45.119 --> 00:33:47.119
of traditions

00:33:47.119 --> 00:33:48.119
which were transmitted,

00:33:48.119 --> 00:33:50.119
there is no machloket,

00:33:50.119 --> 00:33:51.119
and they were transmitted

00:33:51.119 --> 00:33:53.119
at a later time.

00:33:53.119 --> 00:33:55.119
It is like this.

00:33:55.119 --> 00:33:57.119
Nehelakum v'perek eleterefot.

00:33:57.119 --> 00:33:59.119
There is a machloket

00:33:59.119 --> 00:34:01.119
in the third chapter of Holin.

00:34:01.119 --> 00:34:03.119
Al-hotashidra

00:34:03.119 --> 00:34:05.119
shinifsak berubbo.

00:34:05.119 --> 00:34:07.119
The mishnas is like this.

00:34:07.119 --> 00:34:09.120
The spine.

00:34:09.120 --> 00:34:11.120
Hotashidra in Hebrew is

00:34:11.120 --> 00:34:13.120
the spine.

00:34:13.120 --> 00:34:15.120
Shinifsak berubbo.

00:34:15.120 --> 00:34:17.120
That was broken

00:34:17.120 --> 00:34:18.120
in its majority.

00:34:18.120 --> 00:34:19.120
I'll explain everything,

00:34:19.120 --> 00:34:20.120
don't worry.

00:34:20.120 --> 00:34:22.120
Istaref.

00:34:22.120 --> 00:34:23.120
The animal,

00:34:23.120 --> 00:34:25.120
istaref.

00:34:25.120 --> 00:34:27.120
And you could tell,

00:34:27.120 --> 00:34:29.120
I'll tell you how you could tell.

00:34:29.120 --> 00:34:31.120
Now,

00:34:31.120 --> 00:34:33.120
there is a machloket.

00:34:33.120 --> 00:34:35.120
What does it mean,

00:34:35.120 --> 00:34:37.120
the rope?

00:34:37.120 --> 00:34:38.120
The rope, of course,

00:34:38.120 --> 00:34:40.120
we're talking of the vertebrate.

00:34:40.120 --> 00:34:41.120
Yes.

00:34:41.120 --> 00:34:43.120
Of one vertebrate.

00:34:43.120 --> 00:34:45.120
And in the vertebrate,

00:34:45.120 --> 00:34:47.120
inside the vertebrate,

00:34:47.120 --> 00:34:50.120
there is like a gray stuff,

00:34:50.120 --> 00:34:53.120
which is like the gray of the brain.

00:34:53.120 --> 00:34:54.120
Yes.

00:34:54.120 --> 00:34:55.120
And by the way,

00:34:55.120 --> 00:34:56.120
all the neurons,

00:34:56.120 --> 00:34:57.120
how you call it in English?

00:34:57.120 --> 00:34:58.120
Nerves.

00:34:58.120 --> 00:35:00.120
All the nerves

00:35:00.120 --> 00:35:02.120
from the brain are connected

00:35:02.120 --> 00:35:04.120
to the spine.

00:35:04.120 --> 00:35:05.120
Yes.

00:35:05.120 --> 00:35:07.120
And if there is

00:35:07.120 --> 00:35:09.120
one of the brain,

00:35:09.120 --> 00:35:11.120
then there is the brain

00:35:11.120 --> 00:35:13.120
that has no means to send the messages

00:35:13.120 --> 00:35:15.120
to the rest of the body.

00:35:15.120 --> 00:35:16.120
Alright?

00:35:16.120 --> 00:35:18.120
That's the way the brain sends the messages

00:35:18.120 --> 00:35:20.120
to the rest of the body.

00:35:20.120 --> 00:35:22.120
Now, what does it mean,

00:35:22.120 --> 00:35:24.120
rope berubbo, istaref?

00:35:24.120 --> 00:35:25.120
What does it mean, majority?

00:35:25.120 --> 00:35:28.120
Of course, it means the circumference.

00:35:28.120 --> 00:35:29.120
Yes.

00:35:29.120 --> 00:35:30.120
Alright.

00:35:30.120 --> 00:35:31.120
But what?

00:35:31.120 --> 00:35:33.120
There is mahloket.

00:35:33.120 --> 00:35:35.120
One says, daor.

00:35:35.120 --> 00:35:39.120
There is a skin to the spine.

00:35:39.120 --> 00:35:41.120
It has a skin.

00:35:41.120 --> 00:35:43.120
And if the skin is broken,

00:35:43.120 --> 00:35:47.120
the majority of the skin is broken,

00:35:47.120 --> 00:35:50.120
that already makes it taref.

00:35:50.120 --> 00:35:54.120
And another opinion says, no.

00:35:55.120 --> 00:35:56.120
In order to be taref,

00:35:56.120 --> 00:35:58.120
it has to be the rope of the moah,

00:35:58.120 --> 00:36:01.120
already inside.

00:36:01.120 --> 00:36:02.120
Do you understand?

00:36:02.120 --> 00:36:04.120
If it's the rope of the outside,

00:36:04.120 --> 00:36:06.120
but it's not the rope of the inside,

00:36:06.120 --> 00:36:07.120
because it is like this,

00:36:07.120 --> 00:36:09.120
exactly more or less like this.

00:36:09.120 --> 00:36:11.120
There is the rope here, daor.

00:36:11.120 --> 00:36:14.120
And here there is the moah.

00:36:14.120 --> 00:36:15.120
Between this and this,

00:36:15.120 --> 00:36:17.120
there is the vertebrae itself.

00:36:17.120 --> 00:36:19.120
There is the bone.

00:36:19.120 --> 00:36:21.120
So, one opinion says,

00:36:21.120 --> 00:36:25.120
if it's already the rope of this broken,

00:36:25.120 --> 00:36:27.120
I mean torn or broken,

00:36:27.120 --> 00:36:29.120
that is already taref.

00:36:29.120 --> 00:36:30.120
The other says, no.

00:36:30.120 --> 00:36:35.120
It has to be the rope of the moah.

00:36:35.120 --> 00:36:36.120
Yes.

00:36:36.120 --> 00:36:37.120
Wait.

00:36:37.120 --> 00:36:38.120
You're going to see.

00:36:38.120 --> 00:36:39.120
Oh.

00:36:39.120 --> 00:36:41.120
You make a bidikah.

00:36:41.120 --> 00:36:43.120
When do you have to make bidikah?

00:36:43.120 --> 00:36:44.120
For example,

00:36:44.120 --> 00:36:48.120
suppose the animal was thrown against the bag.

00:36:48.120 --> 00:36:49.120
And this has happened many times.

00:36:50.120 --> 00:36:51.120
They do it.

00:36:51.120 --> 00:36:52.120
You know.

00:36:52.120 --> 00:36:54.120
And now it has difficulty in standing up.

00:36:54.120 --> 00:36:55.120
You make shehita,

00:36:55.120 --> 00:36:59.120
but providing that then you have to make a bidikah on the animal,

00:36:59.120 --> 00:37:02.120
because it was thrown.

00:37:02.120 --> 00:37:03.120
Sometimes they throw it, of course.

00:37:03.120 --> 00:37:04.120
And they put it on the ground.

00:37:04.120 --> 00:37:07.120
And they throw it in a way that's against the spine.

00:37:07.120 --> 00:37:08.120
If you throw it against the spine,

00:37:08.120 --> 00:37:09.120
within a second,

00:37:09.120 --> 00:37:13.120
then you make shehita.

00:37:13.120 --> 00:37:14.120
But when you make shehita,

00:37:14.120 --> 00:37:15.120
you have to be bodeg,

00:37:15.120 --> 00:37:19.120
because you may have broken a vertebrate.

00:37:19.120 --> 00:37:20.120
Yes.

00:37:20.120 --> 00:37:22.120
In the first case,

00:37:22.120 --> 00:37:24.120
if it's the outside that's broken,

00:37:24.120 --> 00:37:26.120
it would be pretty easy to see.

00:37:26.120 --> 00:37:27.120
That's right.

00:37:27.120 --> 00:37:28.120
But if it's something inside.

00:37:28.120 --> 00:37:29.120
No.

00:37:29.120 --> 00:37:30.120
But now suppose you see it broken.

00:37:30.120 --> 00:37:32.120
Then the animal is going to be lame.

00:37:32.120 --> 00:37:33.120
No.

00:37:33.120 --> 00:37:34.120
Yeah.

00:37:34.120 --> 00:37:35.120
But it happens.

00:37:35.120 --> 00:37:38.120
This normally happens when you're throwing the animal to shehita.

00:37:38.120 --> 00:37:39.120
Because the Jews,

00:37:39.120 --> 00:37:40.120
in my days,

00:37:40.120 --> 00:37:41.120
now they do it differently.

00:37:41.120 --> 00:37:42.120
They have a machine,

00:37:42.120 --> 00:37:44.120
and they pull the leg of the animal up.

00:37:44.120 --> 00:37:45.120
In my days,

00:37:45.120 --> 00:37:46.120
they didn't use it this way.

00:37:46.120 --> 00:37:49.120
They used to literally bring it to the floor.

00:37:49.120 --> 00:37:50.120
Yes.

00:37:50.120 --> 00:37:51.120
And they used to hold it.

00:37:51.120 --> 00:37:54.120
Two guys to hold the cow,

00:37:54.120 --> 00:37:56.120
and the shohed sits on top of it

00:37:56.120 --> 00:37:57.120
and makes shehita.

00:37:57.120 --> 00:37:58.120
All right?

00:37:58.120 --> 00:38:00.120
That's the way they do it.

00:38:00.120 --> 00:38:02.120
So when you throw the animal,

00:38:02.120 --> 00:38:06.120
sometimes you break the spine.

00:38:06.120 --> 00:38:07.120
You see?

00:38:07.120 --> 00:38:11.120
So today the animal is held from the legs,

00:38:11.120 --> 00:38:15.120
because it is something pulling the animal up.

00:38:15.120 --> 00:38:17.120
But in my days,

00:38:17.120 --> 00:38:18.120
there was no machine.

00:38:18.120 --> 00:38:21.120
They just literally brought the animal down.

00:38:21.120 --> 00:38:24.120
They make it loose the hind legs,

00:38:24.120 --> 00:38:25.120
the balance.

00:38:25.120 --> 00:38:26.120
The animal falls,

00:38:26.120 --> 00:38:27.120
and they stand on top of it.

00:38:27.120 --> 00:38:28.120
They hold it.

00:38:28.120 --> 00:38:29.120
The people,

00:38:29.120 --> 00:38:30.120
they know how to do it.

00:38:30.120 --> 00:38:31.120
Yes.

00:38:31.120 --> 00:38:32.120
Like wrestling.

00:38:32.120 --> 00:38:33.120
Yes.

00:38:33.120 --> 00:38:34.120
Like a rodeo.

00:38:34.120 --> 00:38:35.120
All right?

00:38:35.120 --> 00:38:36.120
And by the way,

00:38:36.120 --> 00:38:37.120
many of the animals on the rodeo,

00:38:37.120 --> 00:38:38.120
you could be sure,

00:38:38.120 --> 00:38:39.120
some of them,

00:38:39.120 --> 00:38:40.120
their spine is broken.

00:38:40.120 --> 00:38:41.120
That's the way they do it

00:38:41.120 --> 00:38:42.120
with the last of the goyim.

00:38:42.120 --> 00:38:43.120
Their spine is broken.

00:38:43.120 --> 00:38:46.120
And so...

00:38:46.120 --> 00:38:47.120
All right.

00:38:47.120 --> 00:38:48.120
So now,

00:38:48.120 --> 00:38:50.120
here it is interesting.

00:38:50.120 --> 00:38:52.120
What the Mishnah says,

00:38:52.120 --> 00:38:55.120
rob chut hashidra.

00:38:55.120 --> 00:38:59.120
Now you see.

00:38:59.120 --> 00:39:00.120
This is an example.

00:39:00.120 --> 00:39:02.120
Shehokim al-pirusha hikar.

00:39:02.120 --> 00:39:03.120
All of them,

00:39:03.120 --> 00:39:04.120
they have the same hikar.

00:39:04.120 --> 00:39:07.120
It has to be the rob chut hashidra.

00:39:07.120 --> 00:39:09.120
The mahlukat is what constitutes rob.

00:39:09.120 --> 00:39:12.120
The outer rob or the inner rob.

00:39:12.120 --> 00:39:13.120
All right?

00:39:13.120 --> 00:39:15.120
Lo ala hikar asmo.

00:39:15.120 --> 00:39:17.120
But on the hikar,

00:39:17.120 --> 00:39:18.120
on the rob that we receive,

00:39:18.120 --> 00:39:20.120
that has to be rob chut hashidra.

00:39:20.120 --> 00:39:22.120
And there is no mahlukat.

00:39:22.120 --> 00:39:23.120
The mahlukat is,

00:39:23.120 --> 00:39:24.120
what does it mean,

00:39:24.120 --> 00:39:26.120
the word rob chut hashidra.

00:39:26.120 --> 00:39:27.120
All right?

00:39:27.120 --> 00:39:30.120
Uma shem ore be yeter se'et,

00:39:30.120 --> 00:39:31.120
be yeter oz,

00:39:31.120 --> 00:39:33.120
sheh hakarim kulam kabala

00:39:33.120 --> 00:39:34.120
min moshe min sinai.

00:39:34.120 --> 00:39:35.120
And the proof,

00:39:35.120 --> 00:39:37.120
that all those principles,

00:39:37.120 --> 00:39:38.120
for instance,

00:39:38.120 --> 00:39:39.120
they have the principle,

00:39:39.120 --> 00:39:42.120
if rob chut hashidra,

00:39:42.120 --> 00:39:43.120
the animal will starve.

00:39:43.120 --> 00:39:44.120
They have the principle.

00:39:44.120 --> 00:39:45.120
What they didn't have,

00:39:45.120 --> 00:39:46.120
that's the principle

00:39:46.120 --> 00:39:47.120
they had at kabala

00:39:47.120 --> 00:39:48.120
min moshe min sinai.

00:39:48.120 --> 00:39:49.120
What they didn't have is,

00:39:49.120 --> 00:39:50.120
what constitutes rob,

00:39:50.120 --> 00:39:52.120
is it the outer circle

00:39:52.120 --> 00:39:53.120
or the inner circle.

00:39:53.120 --> 00:39:55.120
That's the contradiction.

00:39:55.120 --> 00:39:56.120
That's the mahlukat.

00:39:56.120 --> 00:39:57.120
Yes.

00:39:57.120 --> 00:39:58.120
All right?

00:39:58.120 --> 00:39:59.120
Uma shem ore be yeter se'et,

00:39:59.120 --> 00:40:00.120
be yeter oz,

00:40:00.120 --> 00:40:01.120
sheh hakarim kulam kabala

00:40:01.120 --> 00:40:02.120
min moshe min sinai.

00:40:02.120 --> 00:40:03.120
Hush,

00:40:03.120 --> 00:40:04.120
al-tanaim al-asmar,

00:40:04.120 --> 00:40:05.120
in al-hokim be hakarim.

00:40:05.120 --> 00:40:06.120
They never,

00:40:06.120 --> 00:40:07.120
there is mahlukat al-tanaim

00:40:07.120 --> 00:40:08.120
at this point.

00:40:08.120 --> 00:40:09.120
Yes.

00:40:09.120 --> 00:40:10.120
Kimo sheh yokachtim

00:40:10.120 --> 00:40:11.120
min shofar ve'alash,

00:40:11.120 --> 00:40:12.120
as we saw in the case of

00:40:12.120 --> 00:40:13.120
shofar ve'alash,

00:40:13.120 --> 00:40:14.120
there is no mahlukat

00:40:14.120 --> 00:40:15.120
under hakarim.

00:40:15.120 --> 00:40:16.120
All the mahlukat is

00:40:16.120 --> 00:40:17.120
on the interpretations

00:40:17.120 --> 00:40:18.120
or the applications

00:40:18.120 --> 00:40:19.120
of hakarim.

00:40:19.120 --> 00:40:20.120
All right.

00:40:20.120 --> 00:40:23.120
Now,

00:40:23.120 --> 00:40:26.120
it says,

00:40:26.120 --> 00:40:28.120
I think it's late, no?

00:40:28.120 --> 00:40:29.120
Isn't it late?

00:40:29.120 --> 00:40:31.120
I have time.

00:40:31.120 --> 00:40:32.120
I'm married.

00:40:32.120 --> 00:40:33.120
I have twin children.

00:40:33.120 --> 00:40:34.120
I don't have to,

00:40:34.120 --> 00:40:35.120
you know,

00:40:35.120 --> 00:40:36.120
this.

00:40:36.120 --> 00:40:37.120
But,

00:40:37.120 --> 00:40:38.120
if any of you think

00:40:38.120 --> 00:40:39.120
that it's a little bit late,

00:40:39.120 --> 00:40:40.120
don't be shy.

00:40:40.120 --> 00:40:41.120
You're making a messiah,

00:40:41.120 --> 00:40:42.120
you tell him,

00:40:42.120 --> 00:40:43.120
because otherwise

00:40:43.120 --> 00:40:44.120
you're not going to come

00:40:44.120 --> 00:40:45.120
next week.

00:40:45.120 --> 00:40:46.120
So I want you to come.

00:40:46.120 --> 00:40:47.120
So is it,

00:40:47.120 --> 00:40:48.120
do we have five,

00:40:48.120 --> 00:40:49.120
ten more minutes?

00:40:49.120 --> 00:40:50.120
Yes.

00:40:50.120 --> 00:40:51.120
You're sure?

00:40:51.120 --> 00:40:52.120
All right.

00:40:52.120 --> 00:40:53.120
It says,

00:40:53.120 --> 00:40:54.120
dakhina katabia

00:40:54.120 --> 00:40:55.120
ve'atalia,

00:40:55.120 --> 00:40:56.120
I remember when I was

00:40:56.120 --> 00:40:57.120
a younger person,

00:40:57.120 --> 00:40:58.120
sheh masati be

00:40:58.120 --> 00:40:59.120
aktamat al-anbaab,

00:40:59.120 --> 00:41:00.120
that I found

00:41:00.120 --> 00:41:01.120
in the introduction

00:41:01.120 --> 00:41:02.120
to al-anbaab

00:41:02.120 --> 00:41:03.120
that we studied

00:41:03.120 --> 00:41:04.120
last year,

00:41:04.120 --> 00:41:05.120
in which the B'alad

00:41:05.120 --> 00:41:06.120
kotev le'asmo

00:41:06.120 --> 00:41:07.120
kefikohome

00:41:07.120 --> 00:41:08.120
bi'ura tora

00:41:08.120 --> 00:41:09.120
meilchotehah.

00:41:09.120 --> 00:41:10.120
It says that every

00:41:10.120 --> 00:41:11.120
rabbi prior to

00:41:11.120 --> 00:41:12.120
Rabbenu ha'kadosh,

00:41:12.120 --> 00:41:13.120
yes,

00:41:13.120 --> 00:41:14.120
they would write

00:41:14.120 --> 00:41:15.120
privately notes

00:41:15.120 --> 00:41:16.120
about the

00:41:16.120 --> 00:41:17.120
Torah sheh baalpe.

00:41:17.120 --> 00:41:18.120
The notes

00:41:18.120 --> 00:41:19.120
were never published,

00:41:19.120 --> 00:41:20.120
but they were,

00:41:20.120 --> 00:41:21.120
each person,

00:41:21.120 --> 00:41:22.120
because nobody

00:41:22.120 --> 00:41:23.120
could remember everything,

00:41:23.120 --> 00:41:24.120
I mean,

00:41:24.120 --> 00:41:25.120
even the greatest

00:41:25.120 --> 00:41:26.120
memory in,

00:41:26.120 --> 00:41:27.120
you know,

00:41:27.120 --> 00:41:28.120
you can't remember

00:41:28.120 --> 00:41:29.120
everything.

00:41:29.120 --> 00:41:30.120
So it says,

00:41:30.120 --> 00:41:31.120
they used to write

00:41:31.120 --> 00:41:32.120
private notes.

00:41:32.120 --> 00:41:33.120
Everybody has

00:41:33.120 --> 00:41:34.120
to write the

00:41:34.120 --> 00:41:35.120
Torah sheh baalpe.

00:41:35.120 --> 00:41:36.120
All right?

00:41:36.120 --> 00:41:37.120
kemoshe shama,

00:41:37.120 --> 00:41:38.120
omekhah,

00:41:38.120 --> 00:41:39.120
kemoshe shama,

00:41:39.120 --> 00:41:40.120
what he heard

00:41:40.120 --> 00:41:41.120
from his teachers.

00:41:41.120 --> 00:41:42.120
Omedevarim

00:41:42.120 --> 00:41:43.120
shenetahadeshu

00:41:43.120 --> 00:41:44.120
b'khod

00:41:44.120 --> 00:41:45.120
v'khod

00:41:45.120 --> 00:41:46.120
v'khod

00:41:46.120 --> 00:41:47.120
v'khod

00:41:47.120 --> 00:41:48.120
v'khod

00:41:48.120 --> 00:41:49.120
v'khod

00:41:49.120 --> 00:41:50.120
v'khod

00:41:50.120 --> 00:41:51.120
v'khod

00:41:51.120 --> 00:41:52.120
v'khod

00:41:52.120 --> 00:41:53.120
v'khod

00:41:53.120 --> 00:41:54.120
v'khod

00:41:54.120 --> 00:41:55.120
v'khod

00:41:55.120 --> 00:41:56.120
v'khod

00:41:56.120 --> 00:41:57.120
v'khod

00:41:57.120 --> 00:41:58.120
v'khod

00:41:58.120 --> 00:41:59.120
v'khod

00:41:59.120 --> 00:42:00.120
v'khod

00:42:00.120 --> 00:42:01.120
v'khod

00:42:01.120 --> 00:42:02.120
v'khod

00:42:02.120 --> 00:42:03.120
As to the Rash'oth.

00:42:03.120 --> 00:42:04.120
There's 13 ways

00:42:04.120 --> 00:42:06.120
of making the Rash'oth.

00:42:06.120 --> 00:42:07.120
Bezki Muharem

00:42:07.120 --> 00:42:08.120
beddinah galhon

00:42:08.120 --> 00:42:09.120
And

00:42:09.120 --> 00:42:10.120
the Supreme Court

00:42:10.120 --> 00:42:11.120
of Israel

00:42:11.120 --> 00:42:12.120
passed the approval

00:42:12.120 --> 00:42:14.120
on those laws,

00:42:14.120 --> 00:42:15.120
so also they

00:42:15.120 --> 00:42:16.120
wrote down

00:42:16.120 --> 00:42:17.120
each one in his

00:42:17.120 --> 00:42:18.120
notes.

00:42:18.120 --> 00:42:19.120
behini aya

00:42:19.120 --> 00:42:20.120
dabartamith

00:42:20.120 --> 00:42:21.120
and always was like this,

00:42:21.120 --> 00:42:22.120
I'll explain everything,

00:42:22.120 --> 00:42:23.120
don't worry.

00:42:23.120 --> 00:42:24.120
Bey Mohsheki

00:42:24.120 --> 00:42:25.120
bel Torah

00:42:25.120 --> 00:42:26.120
me'senai

00:42:26.120 --> 00:42:27.120
aim cualquier

00:42:27.120 --> 00:42:28.120
shayah

00:42:28.120 --> 00:42:29.120
Now,

00:42:29.120 --> 00:42:30.120
the question that

00:42:30.120 --> 00:42:31.120
I have is the following.

00:42:31.120 --> 00:42:33.120
With all the explanations,

00:42:33.120 --> 00:42:34.120
uklalehain,

00:42:34.120 --> 00:42:36.120
with all the principles,

00:42:36.120 --> 00:42:37.120
upratehain,

00:42:37.120 --> 00:42:38.120
all the details,

00:42:38.120 --> 00:42:39.120
viddikdukehain,

00:42:39.120 --> 00:42:40.120
all the minute,

00:42:40.120 --> 00:42:42.120
the smallest details,

00:42:42.120 --> 00:42:44.120
ekh khatararambam,

00:42:44.120 --> 00:42:45.120
how my mind

00:42:45.120 --> 00:42:46.120
is good right,

00:42:46.120 --> 00:42:47.120
that there were things,

00:42:47.120 --> 00:42:48.120
debarim,

00:42:48.120 --> 00:42:49.120
shleh t'hazdeshu

00:42:49.120 --> 00:42:50.120
bekhodor mador,

00:42:50.120 --> 00:42:51.120
there were things

00:42:51.120 --> 00:42:52.120
that were

00:42:52.120 --> 00:42:53.120
in every generation,

00:42:53.120 --> 00:42:54.120
that were

00:42:54.120 --> 00:42:55.120
new,

00:42:55.120 --> 00:42:56.120
and also,

00:42:56.120 --> 00:42:58.120
ma salikha ya l'hidush,

00:42:58.120 --> 00:42:59.120
why is it

00:42:59.120 --> 00:43:00.120
necessary

00:43:00.120 --> 00:43:01.120
to have

00:43:01.120 --> 00:43:02.120
a hidush?

00:43:02.120 --> 00:43:03.120
Now,

00:43:03.120 --> 00:43:04.120
briefly,

00:43:04.120 --> 00:43:05.120
this is,

00:43:05.120 --> 00:43:06.120
you see,

00:43:06.120 --> 00:43:07.120
on the basis

00:43:07.120 --> 00:43:08.120
of these questions,

00:43:08.120 --> 00:43:09.120
I learned,

00:43:09.120 --> 00:43:10.120
I became,

00:43:10.120 --> 00:43:11.120
my mind became,

00:43:11.120 --> 00:43:12.120
you know,

00:43:12.120 --> 00:43:13.120
I learned from

00:43:13.120 --> 00:43:14.120
these questions,

00:43:14.120 --> 00:43:15.120
from the

00:43:15.120 --> 00:43:16.120
Hakam David Neto,

00:43:16.120 --> 00:43:17.120
and of course,

00:43:17.120 --> 00:43:18.120
I had my book,

00:43:18.120 --> 00:43:19.120
Iyurim Bebishe Torah

00:43:19.120 --> 00:43:20.120
Aramban,

00:43:20.120 --> 00:43:21.120
which I devote

00:43:21.120 --> 00:43:22.120
to my,

00:43:22.120 --> 00:43:23.120
almost,

00:43:23.120 --> 00:43:24.120
the majority

00:43:24.120 --> 00:43:25.120
of the book

00:43:25.120 --> 00:43:26.120
to answer

00:43:26.120 --> 00:43:27.120
this question,

00:43:27.120 --> 00:43:28.120
because they are

00:43:28.120 --> 00:43:29.120
very important questions,

00:43:29.120 --> 00:43:30.120
very simple.

00:43:30.120 --> 00:43:31.120
And I,

00:43:31.120 --> 00:43:32.120
Baruch Hashem,

00:43:32.120 --> 00:43:33.120
afterwards,

00:43:33.120 --> 00:43:34.120
I wrote about it

00:43:34.120 --> 00:43:35.120
in Hebrew,

00:43:35.120 --> 00:43:36.120
and also,

00:43:36.120 --> 00:43:37.120
I wrote about it

00:43:37.120 --> 00:43:38.120
in English,

00:43:38.120 --> 00:43:39.120
in several articles,

00:43:39.120 --> 00:43:40.120
and also,

00:43:40.120 --> 00:43:41.120
I have,

00:43:41.120 --> 00:43:42.120
in French,

00:43:42.120 --> 00:43:43.120
I have a long,

00:43:43.120 --> 00:43:44.120
long,

00:43:44.120 --> 00:43:45.120
135,

00:43:45.120 --> 00:43:46.120
140 pages article

00:43:46.120 --> 00:43:47.120
in French

00:43:47.120 --> 00:43:48.120
about this thing,

00:43:48.120 --> 00:43:49.120
and,

00:43:49.120 --> 00:43:50.120
no, no,

00:43:50.120 --> 00:43:51.120
because I'm,

00:43:51.120 --> 00:43:52.120
it's very,

00:43:52.120 --> 00:43:53.120
not everybody

00:43:53.120 --> 00:43:54.120
knows it,

00:43:54.120 --> 00:43:55.120
you know,

00:43:55.120 --> 00:43:56.120
and I develop it,

00:43:56.120 --> 00:43:57.120
and I develop it

00:43:57.120 --> 00:43:58.120
in a legal sense.

00:43:58.120 --> 00:43:59.120
So,

00:43:59.120 --> 00:44:00.120
this is the Torah.

00:44:00.120 --> 00:44:01.120
And the Torah,

00:44:01.120 --> 00:44:02.120
it's explicit,

00:44:02.120 --> 00:44:03.120
that when Borei HaOlam

00:44:03.120 --> 00:44:04.120
told Moshe Rabbeinu

00:44:04.120 --> 00:44:05.120
Tefillin,

00:44:05.120 --> 00:44:06.120
he told him,

00:44:06.120 --> 00:44:07.120
Tefillin has to be square,

00:44:07.120 --> 00:44:08.120
has to be black,

00:44:08.120 --> 00:44:09.120
has to be,

00:44:09.120 --> 00:44:10.120
this,

00:44:10.120 --> 00:44:11.120
all the details.

00:44:11.120 --> 00:44:12.120
Fine.

00:44:12.120 --> 00:44:13.120
But,

00:44:13.120 --> 00:44:14.120
the Bet Taddin,

00:44:14.120 --> 00:44:15.120
the Supreme Court

00:44:15.120 --> 00:44:16.120
of Israel,

00:44:16.120 --> 00:44:17.120
has

00:44:17.120 --> 00:44:18.120
three realms

00:44:18.120 --> 00:44:19.120
of authority.

00:44:19.120 --> 00:44:20.120
Three,

00:44:20.120 --> 00:44:23.120
which are very important.

00:44:23.120 --> 00:44:26.120
Realm number one,

00:44:26.120 --> 00:44:27.120
the transmission

00:44:27.120 --> 00:44:28.120
of those laws

00:44:28.120 --> 00:44:29.120
that we get

00:44:29.120 --> 00:44:30.120
from Moshe Messinai.

00:44:30.120 --> 00:44:33.120
And only the Bet Din HaGadol

00:44:33.120 --> 00:44:34.120
has the right

00:44:34.120 --> 00:44:35.120
to tell you,

00:44:35.120 --> 00:44:36.120
this we receive

00:44:36.120 --> 00:44:39.120
from Moshe Messinai.

00:44:39.120 --> 00:44:40.120
I'll give you an example,

00:44:40.120 --> 00:44:41.120
the laws of Tefillin,

00:44:41.120 --> 00:44:43.120
the laws of Sukkah.

00:44:43.120 --> 00:44:44.120
This was transmitted

00:44:44.120 --> 00:44:45.120
to us through

00:44:45.120 --> 00:44:46.120
Bet Din HaGadol,

00:44:46.120 --> 00:44:47.120
and Bet Din HaGadol,

00:44:47.120 --> 00:44:48.120
which is the Supreme Court

00:44:48.120 --> 00:44:50.120
of Israel,

00:44:50.120 --> 00:44:51.120
had the authority

00:44:51.120 --> 00:44:52.120
to transmit

00:44:52.120 --> 00:44:53.120
the Torah

00:44:53.120 --> 00:44:54.120
to Moshe Messinai.

00:44:54.120 --> 00:44:55.120
Moshe Gibel,

00:44:55.120 --> 00:44:56.120
the minister of Torah,

00:44:56.120 --> 00:44:57.120
who was the head

00:44:57.120 --> 00:44:58.120
of the Jewish nation,

00:44:58.120 --> 00:45:05.120
the Jewish Supreme Court.

00:45:05.120 --> 00:45:06.120
Fine.

00:45:06.120 --> 00:45:07.120
So we have

00:45:07.120 --> 00:45:10.120
one realm.

00:45:10.120 --> 00:45:12.120
Second,

00:45:12.120 --> 00:45:14.120
they have the right

00:45:14.120 --> 00:45:17.120
to interpret the Pasuk.

00:45:17.120 --> 00:45:20.120
On their own.

00:45:20.120 --> 00:45:21.120
Because,

00:45:21.120 --> 00:45:22.120
no matter

00:45:22.120 --> 00:45:24.120
who you are,

00:45:25.120 --> 00:45:28.120
the world is constantly changing.

00:45:28.120 --> 00:45:30.120
And it is up to

00:45:30.120 --> 00:45:32.120
the Hachamim

00:45:32.120 --> 00:45:35.120
to interpret.

00:45:35.120 --> 00:45:37.120
This interpretation

00:45:37.120 --> 00:45:41.120
becomes law

00:45:41.120 --> 00:45:42.120
when it is done

00:45:42.120 --> 00:45:43.120
through the Yud Giman,

00:45:43.120 --> 00:45:45.120
there is 13 Yud Giman

00:45:45.120 --> 00:45:46.120
Middot Shatonar

00:45:46.120 --> 00:45:47.120
in the direction.

00:45:47.120 --> 00:45:48.120
But,

00:45:48.120 --> 00:45:49.120
it has to be submitted

00:45:49.120 --> 00:45:52.120
to a vote,

00:45:52.120 --> 00:45:53.120
and the Sanhedrin

00:45:53.120 --> 00:45:55.120
has to agree upon it.

00:45:55.120 --> 00:45:56.120
And therefore,

00:45:56.120 --> 00:45:57.120
that is why

00:45:57.120 --> 00:45:58.120
I make it also

00:45:58.120 --> 00:45:59.120
in my Cardozo Law Review,

00:45:59.120 --> 00:46:01.120
I discuss very extensively

00:46:01.120 --> 00:46:02.120
this point.

00:46:02.120 --> 00:46:03.120
But then,

00:46:03.120 --> 00:46:04.120
it is law,

00:46:04.120 --> 00:46:05.120
not by virtue

00:46:05.120 --> 00:46:06.120
of the exegesis

00:46:06.120 --> 00:46:08.120
of the interpretation,

00:46:08.120 --> 00:46:09.120
but by virtue

00:46:09.120 --> 00:46:10.120
of being passed

00:46:10.120 --> 00:46:11.120
by the Sanhedrin.

00:46:11.120 --> 00:46:12.120
In other words,

00:46:12.120 --> 00:46:13.120
you could be the greatest

00:46:13.120 --> 00:46:14.120
Darshan in the world.

00:46:14.120 --> 00:46:15.120
Alright?

00:46:15.120 --> 00:46:16.120
You could say

00:46:16.120 --> 00:46:17.120
the Darshan,

00:46:17.120 --> 00:46:18.120
and nobody,

00:46:18.120 --> 00:46:19.120
the Sanhedrin doesn't want to,

00:46:19.120 --> 00:46:23.120
does not agree with it.

00:46:23.120 --> 00:46:24.120
It's not a law.

00:46:24.120 --> 00:46:27.120
It becomes a law only

00:46:27.120 --> 00:46:29.120
if it is approved

00:46:29.120 --> 00:46:31.120
by the Sanhedrin.

00:46:31.120 --> 00:46:32.120
And because it depends

00:46:32.120 --> 00:46:35.120
on the Sanhedrin,

00:46:35.120 --> 00:46:37.120
tomorrow another Sanhedrin

00:46:37.120 --> 00:46:38.120
could say,

00:46:38.120 --> 00:46:41.120
we don't like this law.

00:46:41.120 --> 00:46:43.120
And they could abrogate it.

00:46:43.120 --> 00:46:45.120
Because that law

00:46:45.120 --> 00:46:47.120
came through legislation,

00:46:47.120 --> 00:46:49.120
not through tradition.

00:46:49.120 --> 00:46:51.120
You understand?

00:46:51.120 --> 00:46:52.120
I'm going to give you

00:46:52.120 --> 00:46:53.120
some examples.

00:46:53.120 --> 00:46:54.120
I'll give you some examples

00:46:54.120 --> 00:46:56.120
in a minute.

00:46:56.120 --> 00:46:57.120
And finally,

00:46:57.120 --> 00:46:58.120
then there are laws

00:46:58.120 --> 00:46:59.120
which have nothing to do

00:46:59.120 --> 00:47:02.120
with the Pasuk of the Torah.

00:47:02.120 --> 00:47:03.120
They are Takanot and Gezerot,

00:47:03.120 --> 00:47:05.120
Sayagla Torah.

00:47:05.120 --> 00:47:08.120
And that's the third realm

00:47:08.120 --> 00:47:09.120
of the Bedeen.

00:47:09.120 --> 00:47:12.120
So,

00:47:12.120 --> 00:47:14.120
about buying and selling

00:47:14.120 --> 00:47:15.120
a Shabbat.

00:47:15.120 --> 00:47:17.120
It's not written in no place.

00:47:17.120 --> 00:47:20.120
The Chumash never says,

00:47:20.120 --> 00:47:22.120
Lotikah, Velotimkor.

00:47:22.120 --> 00:47:24.120
They don't say this.

00:47:24.120 --> 00:47:26.120
If you look in the Gemara,

00:47:26.120 --> 00:47:28.120
the Gemara says explicitly,

00:47:28.120 --> 00:47:30.120
explicitly,

00:47:30.120 --> 00:47:34.120
that this is a rabbinic institution.

00:47:34.120 --> 00:47:35.120
Why?

00:47:35.120 --> 00:47:36.120
It's simple.

00:47:36.120 --> 00:47:38.120
In the time of the Torah,

00:47:38.120 --> 00:47:39.120
there was no Mecca, Hamam,

00:47:39.120 --> 00:47:41.120
because we were farmers.

00:47:41.120 --> 00:47:45.120
We were not business people.

00:47:45.120 --> 00:47:47.120
So, the 39 works

00:47:47.120 --> 00:47:48.120
have nothing to do

00:47:48.120 --> 00:47:50.120
with buying and selling.

00:47:50.120 --> 00:47:51.120
You see?

00:47:51.120 --> 00:47:52.120
The Hagamim,

00:47:52.120 --> 00:47:54.120
in their infinite wisdom,

00:47:54.120 --> 00:47:55.120
they say,

00:47:55.120 --> 00:47:56.120
Mecca, Hamam,

00:47:56.120 --> 00:47:57.120
because they forbid it.

00:47:57.120 --> 00:47:58.120
You see?

00:47:58.120 --> 00:47:59.120
Now,

00:47:59.120 --> 00:48:01.120
this is a new invention.

00:48:01.120 --> 00:48:02.120
But they have the right

00:48:02.120 --> 00:48:04.120
to do that.

00:48:04.120 --> 00:48:06.120
No society,

00:48:06.120 --> 00:48:08.120
yes,

00:48:08.120 --> 00:48:10.120
can stand still.

00:48:10.120 --> 00:48:12.120
There was always changes.

00:48:12.120 --> 00:48:13.120
And when there were changes,

00:48:13.120 --> 00:48:15.120
they made derashot.

00:48:15.120 --> 00:48:17.120
Derashot to accommodate to this.

00:48:17.120 --> 00:48:18.120
And therefore, as I say,

00:48:18.120 --> 00:48:19.120
in a derasha,

00:48:19.120 --> 00:48:20.120
in theory,

00:48:20.120 --> 00:48:21.120
another beddin,

00:48:21.120 --> 00:48:22.120
could this.

00:48:22.120 --> 00:48:23.120
And now, I'll give you an example

00:48:23.120 --> 00:48:24.120
of Sayyag, the Torah.

00:48:24.120 --> 00:48:25.120
And that's it.

00:48:25.120 --> 00:48:27.120
And then I'll try to answer the question.

00:48:27.120 --> 00:48:28.120
The Torah says,

00:48:28.120 --> 00:48:29.120
Lotavashal gedibah,

00:48:29.120 --> 00:48:30.120
halebim mo.

00:48:30.120 --> 00:48:34.120
It has to be a four-legged animal.

00:48:34.120 --> 00:48:35.120
Chicken,

00:48:35.120 --> 00:48:36.120
no place,

00:48:36.120 --> 00:48:39.120
it says it's halal to eat with milk.

00:48:39.120 --> 00:48:41.120
But,

00:48:41.120 --> 00:48:43.120
our society changed.

00:48:43.120 --> 00:48:45.120
And people, in their mind,

00:48:45.120 --> 00:48:46.120
they didn't distinguish,

00:48:46.120 --> 00:48:48.120
it made no sense to them,

00:48:48.120 --> 00:48:49.120
that you're going to eat,

00:48:49.120 --> 00:48:51.120
that chicken is permitted,

00:48:51.120 --> 00:48:54.120
and with milk,

00:48:54.120 --> 00:48:57.120
and cow is forbidden.

00:48:57.120 --> 00:48:58.120
So Hamam says,

00:48:58.120 --> 00:48:59.120
Sayyag, the Torah,

00:48:59.120 --> 00:49:01.120
we forbidden also chicken,

00:49:01.120 --> 00:49:02.120
to eat with milk.

00:49:02.120 --> 00:49:03.120
That's Sayyag, the Torah.

00:49:03.120 --> 00:49:04.120
You understand?

00:49:04.120 --> 00:49:05.120
In order to protect

00:49:05.120 --> 00:49:06.120
a legislation from the Torah.

00:49:06.120 --> 00:49:07.120
The Torah says,

00:49:07.120 --> 00:49:08.120
Lotavashal gedibah, halebim mo.

00:49:08.120 --> 00:49:09.120
If you're going to permit

00:49:09.120 --> 00:49:10.120
the chicken,

00:49:10.120 --> 00:49:11.120
in the mind of the people,

00:49:11.120 --> 00:49:12.120
eventually they're going to

00:49:12.120 --> 00:49:13.120
go and eat and get.

00:49:13.120 --> 00:49:14.120
That's what the Hachamim,

00:49:14.120 --> 00:49:15.120
they believe,

00:49:15.120 --> 00:49:16.120
and therefore they forbid

00:49:16.120 --> 00:49:17.120
the chicken,

00:49:17.120 --> 00:49:18.120
in order to protect

00:49:18.120 --> 00:49:20.120
the meat.

00:49:20.120 --> 00:49:21.120
And then you have

00:49:21.120 --> 00:49:22.120
another laws,

00:49:22.120 --> 00:49:23.120
like the laws, for instance,

00:49:23.120 --> 00:49:24.120
of Netyat Yalaim.

00:49:24.120 --> 00:49:25.120
That's an invention of the Rabbis.

00:49:25.120 --> 00:49:27.120
Hachamim, they have the right

00:49:27.120 --> 00:49:28.120
to do that.

00:49:28.120 --> 00:49:29.120
You see?

00:49:29.120 --> 00:49:30.120
They have the invention

00:49:30.120 --> 00:49:32.120
of Mecca Hamamka.

00:49:32.120 --> 00:49:34.120
It's only with Rabbanan.

00:49:34.120 --> 00:49:37.120
Hamam means to sell and buy.

00:49:38.120 --> 00:49:39.120
They forbid it.

00:49:39.120 --> 00:49:40.120
So the Hachamim,

00:49:40.120 --> 00:49:41.120
they have the right

00:49:41.120 --> 00:49:42.120
to do it.

00:49:42.120 --> 00:49:43.120
But, because this is

00:49:43.120 --> 00:49:44.120
a Rabbinic institution,

00:49:44.120 --> 00:49:45.120
that's the point I'm making

00:49:45.120 --> 00:49:46.120
in my ayyunim,

00:49:46.120 --> 00:49:47.120
and I show it,

00:49:47.120 --> 00:49:49.120
another court

00:49:49.120 --> 00:49:51.120
could abrogate it.

00:49:51.120 --> 00:49:52.120
You see?

00:49:52.120 --> 00:49:53.120
Isaac.

00:49:53.120 --> 00:49:54.120
I get it.

00:49:54.120 --> 00:49:55.120
Here.

00:49:58.120 --> 00:49:59.120
Get a banan.

00:49:59.120 --> 00:50:00.120
Get a banan.

00:50:00.120 --> 00:50:01.120
But it's a cigarette.

00:50:01.120 --> 00:50:02.120
Ah, that's not important.

00:50:02.120 --> 00:50:03.120
Haram Bam is a question.

00:50:03.120 --> 00:50:05.120
Of course, the Gemara in Shabbat

00:50:05.120 --> 00:50:06.120
is the question.

00:50:06.120 --> 00:50:07.120
And Haram Bam takes it as it is.

00:50:07.120 --> 00:50:08.120
Because,

00:50:08.120 --> 00:50:09.120
here comes the point

00:50:09.120 --> 00:50:11.120
which people do not understand.

00:50:11.120 --> 00:50:13.120
There is 630 misbot.

00:50:15.120 --> 00:50:17.120
If you make any of the

00:50:17.120 --> 00:50:19.120
misbot ase,

00:50:19.120 --> 00:50:21.120
yes,

00:50:21.120 --> 00:50:22.120
then you have

00:50:22.120 --> 00:50:24.120
to make a barakah.

00:50:25.120 --> 00:50:26.120
One of the misbot

00:50:26.120 --> 00:50:28.120
is to listen to the Rabbis.

00:50:28.120 --> 00:50:30.120
Al piya tora shi yoruha.

00:50:30.120 --> 00:50:31.120
Therefore, when I am making

00:50:31.120 --> 00:50:32.120
a tirat yadaim,

00:50:32.120 --> 00:50:33.120
Haram Bam says,

00:50:33.120 --> 00:50:34.120
you are indirectly making

00:50:34.120 --> 00:50:36.120
a misamina tora,

00:50:36.120 --> 00:50:37.120
which is

00:50:37.120 --> 00:50:38.120
listening to

00:50:38.120 --> 00:50:40.120
the bisak of the hakamim.

00:50:40.120 --> 00:50:41.120
That's why people

00:50:41.120 --> 00:50:42.120
don't understand.

00:50:42.120 --> 00:50:43.120
For instance,

00:50:43.120 --> 00:50:45.120
I don't shave in Hulamu'it.

00:50:45.120 --> 00:50:46.120
And really, it's difficult

00:50:46.120 --> 00:50:47.120
for me not to shave

00:50:47.120 --> 00:50:48.120
because I feel awkward.

00:50:48.120 --> 00:50:49.120
Yes?

00:50:49.120 --> 00:50:51.120
But,

00:50:51.120 --> 00:50:53.120
this means because

00:50:53.120 --> 00:50:55.120
we are obeying, still,

00:50:55.120 --> 00:50:57.120
the laws of the hakamim.

00:50:57.120 --> 00:50:58.120
We are obeying the laws

00:50:58.120 --> 00:50:59.120
of the hakamim.

00:50:59.120 --> 00:51:00.120
The hakamim says,

00:51:00.120 --> 00:51:01.120
we obey the laws of the hakamim.

00:51:01.120 --> 00:51:02.120
You say, oh,

00:51:02.120 --> 00:51:03.120
I don't know.

00:51:03.120 --> 00:51:04.120
The tirat yadaim.

00:51:04.120 --> 00:51:05.120
There is no police.

00:51:05.120 --> 00:51:06.120
There is no guns

00:51:06.120 --> 00:51:07.120
in our house.

00:51:07.120 --> 00:51:08.120
And we obey those laws

00:51:08.120 --> 00:51:09.120
more than the laws

00:51:09.120 --> 00:51:10.120
of the government

00:51:10.120 --> 00:51:11.120
with all the police

00:51:11.120 --> 00:51:12.120
and so on.

00:51:12.120 --> 00:51:13.120
Why?

00:51:13.120 --> 00:51:14.120
We believe in the institutions.

00:51:14.120 --> 00:51:15.120
So, therefore,

00:51:15.120 --> 00:51:16.120
whenever we make

00:51:16.120 --> 00:51:17.120
a tirat yadaim,

00:51:17.120 --> 00:51:18.120
we say,

00:51:18.120 --> 00:51:19.120
I am a tirat yadaim

00:51:19.120 --> 00:51:20.120
because

00:51:20.120 --> 00:51:21.120
I am a tirat yadaim

00:51:21.120 --> 00:51:22.120
because

00:51:22.120 --> 00:51:23.120
I am a tirat yadaim.

00:51:23.120 --> 00:51:24.120
Al piya tora shi yoruha.

00:51:24.120 --> 00:51:25.120
The same thing with

00:51:25.120 --> 00:51:26.120
halal.

00:51:26.120 --> 00:51:27.120
Haram Bam says,

00:51:27.120 --> 00:51:28.120
halal is only

00:51:28.120 --> 00:51:29.120
with Rabbana.

00:51:29.120 --> 00:51:30.120
Some people say,

00:51:30.120 --> 00:51:31.120
I am a halal.

00:51:31.120 --> 00:51:32.120
Some people say,

00:51:32.120 --> 00:51:33.120
I am a halal.

00:51:33.120 --> 00:51:34.120
Haram Bam says,

00:51:34.120 --> 00:51:35.120
yes,

00:51:35.120 --> 00:51:36.120
like Hanukkah

00:51:36.120 --> 00:51:37.120
because this was

00:51:37.120 --> 00:51:38.120
instituted by

00:51:38.120 --> 00:51:39.120
a bona fide

00:51:39.120 --> 00:51:40.120
beddeen.

00:51:40.120 --> 00:51:41.120
This beddeen,

00:51:41.120 --> 00:51:42.120
in our estimation,

00:51:42.120 --> 00:51:43.120
it ended

00:51:43.120 --> 00:51:44.120
with the Gemara.

00:51:44.120 --> 00:51:45.120
The Gemara,

00:51:45.120 --> 00:51:46.120
Rabbina bin Rashid,

00:51:46.120 --> 00:51:47.120
was the last beddeen

00:51:47.120 --> 00:51:48.120
had gathered

00:51:48.120 --> 00:51:49.120
that we had

00:51:49.120 --> 00:51:50.120
with the authority

00:51:50.120 --> 00:51:51.120
to promulgate

00:51:51.120 --> 00:51:52.120
and make such laws.

00:51:52.120 --> 00:51:53.120
Ishaq.

00:51:53.120 --> 00:51:54.120
The second one

00:51:54.120 --> 00:51:55.120
is taking away

00:51:55.120 --> 00:51:56.120
the marriage

00:51:56.120 --> 00:51:57.120
of marriage

00:51:57.120 --> 00:51:58.120
to the government

00:51:58.120 --> 00:51:59.120
of Allah.

00:51:59.120 --> 00:52:00.120
Alright.

00:52:01.120 --> 00:52:02.120
No, no.

00:52:02.120 --> 00:52:03.120
Piriyab-e-Ribiya

00:52:03.120 --> 00:52:04.120
is minat-tora.

00:52:04.120 --> 00:52:05.120
Peru, Urubu,

00:52:05.120 --> 00:52:06.120
Milweta,

00:52:06.120 --> 00:52:07.120
I don't know.

00:52:07.120 --> 00:52:08.120
While Haram Bam

00:52:08.120 --> 00:52:09.120
says it is not

00:52:09.120 --> 00:52:10.120
minat-tora.

00:52:10.120 --> 00:52:11.120
Haram Bam says

00:52:11.120 --> 00:52:12.120
like this.

00:52:12.120 --> 00:52:13.120
The Torah says

00:52:13.120 --> 00:52:14.120
ki kah ishaq.

00:52:14.120 --> 00:52:15.120
When a man

00:52:15.120 --> 00:52:16.120
takes a woman

00:52:16.120 --> 00:52:17.120
for a wife.

00:52:17.120 --> 00:52:18.120
And if you

00:52:18.120 --> 00:52:19.120
pay attention,

00:52:19.120 --> 00:52:20.120
in the Torah,

00:52:20.120 --> 00:52:21.120
the only thing

00:52:21.120 --> 00:52:22.120
that has to do

00:52:22.120 --> 00:52:23.120
with marriage,

00:52:23.120 --> 00:52:24.120
there are two things

00:52:24.120 --> 00:52:25.120
that have to do

00:52:25.120 --> 00:52:26.120
with marriage.

00:52:26.120 --> 00:52:27.120
One is

00:52:27.120 --> 00:52:28.120
being.

00:52:28.120 --> 00:52:29.120
Being

00:52:29.120 --> 00:52:30.120
One is

00:52:30.120 --> 00:52:31.120
being.

00:52:31.120 --> 00:52:32.120
Intercourse.

00:52:32.120 --> 00:52:33.120
For instance,

00:52:33.120 --> 00:52:34.120
in America.

00:52:34.120 --> 00:52:35.120
In America,

00:52:35.120 --> 00:52:36.120
marriage is only

00:52:36.120 --> 00:52:37.120
through intercourse.

00:52:37.120 --> 00:52:38.120
You know this.

00:52:38.120 --> 00:52:39.120
If you have

00:52:39.120 --> 00:52:40.120
no intercourse,

00:52:40.120 --> 00:52:41.120
the marriage is not

00:52:41.120 --> 00:52:42.120
consummated.

00:52:42.120 --> 00:52:43.120
Because according

00:52:43.120 --> 00:52:44.120
to them,

00:52:44.120 --> 00:52:45.120
it is only

00:52:45.120 --> 00:52:46.120
mikat-tashim

00:52:46.120 --> 00:52:47.120
be-bia.

00:52:47.120 --> 00:52:48.120
I want you

00:52:48.120 --> 00:52:49.120
to know the law.

00:52:49.120 --> 00:52:50.120
We are going

00:52:50.120 --> 00:52:51.120
to know the law.

00:52:51.120 --> 00:52:52.120
According to

00:52:52.120 --> 00:52:53.120
the Torah,

00:52:53.120 --> 00:52:54.120
being

00:52:54.120 --> 00:52:55.120
is very clear.

00:52:55.120 --> 00:52:56.120
And the other

00:52:56.120 --> 00:52:57.120
place which is

00:52:57.120 --> 00:52:58.120
implicit is

00:52:58.120 --> 00:52:59.120
shetar.

00:52:59.120 --> 00:53:00.120
Because

00:53:00.120 --> 00:53:01.120
in Ged,

00:53:01.120 --> 00:53:02.120
be-yasea

00:53:02.120 --> 00:53:03.120
be-hayata

00:53:03.120 --> 00:53:04.120
le-ish aher.

00:53:04.120 --> 00:53:05.120
So you see

00:53:05.120 --> 00:53:06.120
that the yasea

00:53:06.120 --> 00:53:07.120
and the hayata

00:53:07.120 --> 00:53:08.120
is the same way.

00:53:08.120 --> 00:53:09.120
You do it

00:53:09.120 --> 00:53:10.120
with shetar.

00:53:10.120 --> 00:53:11.120
The way we do it

00:53:11.120 --> 00:53:12.120
now,

00:53:12.120 --> 00:53:13.120
with money,

00:53:13.120 --> 00:53:14.120
is not written

00:53:14.120 --> 00:53:15.120
in the Torah.

00:53:15.120 --> 00:53:16.120
Is not written

00:53:16.120 --> 00:53:17.120
in the Torah.

00:53:17.120 --> 00:53:18.120
So therefore,

00:53:18.120 --> 00:53:19.120
harambam,

00:53:19.120 --> 00:53:20.120
I have

00:53:20.120 --> 00:53:21.120
extensively

00:53:21.120 --> 00:53:22.120
written about

00:53:22.120 --> 00:53:23.120
this in

00:53:23.120 --> 00:53:24.120
my

00:53:24.120 --> 00:53:25.120
ayoni

00:53:25.120 --> 00:53:26.120
be-shetar

00:53:26.120 --> 00:53:27.120
harambam.

00:53:28.120 --> 00:53:29.120
Harambam

00:53:29.120 --> 00:53:30.120
says,

00:53:30.120 --> 00:53:31.120
this is only

00:53:31.120 --> 00:53:32.120
the rabbanaan.

00:53:32.120 --> 00:53:33.120
What does it mean

00:53:33.120 --> 00:53:34.120
why it says

00:53:34.120 --> 00:53:35.120
the rabbanaan?

00:53:35.120 --> 00:53:36.120
The institution

00:53:36.120 --> 00:53:37.120
that you do it

00:53:37.120 --> 00:53:38.120
with money,

00:53:38.120 --> 00:53:39.120
that is a

00:53:39.120 --> 00:53:40.120
rabbinic institution.

00:53:40.120 --> 00:53:41.120
Why?

00:53:41.120 --> 00:53:42.120
In the

00:53:42.120 --> 00:53:43.120
infinite wisdom,

00:53:43.120 --> 00:53:44.120
the Hakamin thought

00:53:44.120 --> 00:53:45.120
that be-yas should not

00:53:45.120 --> 00:53:46.120
be the only way

00:53:46.120 --> 00:53:47.120
to get married.

00:53:47.120 --> 00:53:48.120
Shetar,

00:53:48.120 --> 00:53:49.120
not every

00:53:49.120 --> 00:53:50.120
community

00:53:50.120 --> 00:53:51.120
had a

00:53:51.120 --> 00:53:52.120
bona fide

00:53:52.120 --> 00:53:53.120
scribe,

00:53:53.120 --> 00:53:54.120
which is

00:53:54.120 --> 00:53:55.120
like a,

00:53:55.120 --> 00:53:56.120
to be a scribe

00:53:56.120 --> 00:53:57.120
in Jewish law

00:53:57.120 --> 00:53:58.120
is to be like a

00:53:58.120 --> 00:53:59.120
corporate lawyer

00:53:59.120 --> 00:54:00.120
in America.

00:54:00.120 --> 00:54:01.120
You know,

00:54:01.120 --> 00:54:02.120
because you have to know

00:54:02.120 --> 00:54:03.120
all the ins and outs

00:54:03.120 --> 00:54:04.120
of a shetar,

00:54:04.120 --> 00:54:05.120
which is not so easy.

00:54:05.120 --> 00:54:06.120
And therefore,

00:54:06.120 --> 00:54:07.120
they instituted

00:54:07.120 --> 00:54:08.120
a third way to marry,

00:54:08.120 --> 00:54:09.120
through kesef.

00:54:09.120 --> 00:54:10.120
Now,

00:54:10.120 --> 00:54:11.120
that institution,

00:54:11.120 --> 00:54:12.120
which is

00:54:12.120 --> 00:54:13.120
mik-kesef,

00:54:13.120 --> 00:54:14.120
that is a

00:54:14.120 --> 00:54:15.120
rabbinic institution.

00:54:15.120 --> 00:54:16.120
They do it

00:54:16.120 --> 00:54:17.120
through derasha.

00:54:17.120 --> 00:54:18.120
And that's

00:54:18.120 --> 00:54:19.120
the point.

00:54:19.120 --> 00:54:20.120
The Hakamin,

00:54:20.120 --> 00:54:21.120
they have the right

00:54:21.120 --> 00:54:22.120
to make a derasha,

00:54:22.120 --> 00:54:23.120
to adjust.

00:54:23.120 --> 00:54:24.120
You know.

00:54:25.120 --> 00:54:26.120
My question is,

00:54:26.120 --> 00:54:27.120
if,

00:54:27.120 --> 00:54:28.120
if,

00:54:28.120 --> 00:54:29.120
if we have

00:54:29.120 --> 00:54:30.120
an idea,

00:54:30.120 --> 00:54:31.120
that we could go like that,

00:54:31.120 --> 00:54:32.120
but,

00:54:32.120 --> 00:54:33.120
we get there,

00:54:33.120 --> 00:54:34.120
so that there are

00:54:34.120 --> 00:54:35.120
enough.

00:54:35.120 --> 00:54:36.120
We don't make,

00:54:36.120 --> 00:54:37.120
we don't make

00:54:37.120 --> 00:54:38.120
conditions for that.

00:54:38.120 --> 00:54:39.120
Because it's

00:54:39.120 --> 00:54:40.120
mekkah humemkat.

00:54:40.120 --> 00:54:41.120
Exactly.

00:54:41.120 --> 00:54:42.120
The very sense,

00:54:42.120 --> 00:54:43.120
the very,

00:54:43.120 --> 00:54:44.120
I mean,

00:54:44.120 --> 00:54:45.120
the rabbis are very subtle

00:54:45.120 --> 00:54:46.120
and very intelligent.

00:54:46.120 --> 00:54:47.120
The very,

00:54:47.120 --> 00:54:48.120
the very fact

00:54:48.120 --> 00:54:49.120
that they tell you

00:54:49.120 --> 00:54:50.120
that you're not

00:54:50.120 --> 00:54:51.120
permitted to marry

00:54:51.120 --> 00:54:52.120
on Shabbat

00:54:52.120 --> 00:54:53.120
because mekkah humemkat,

00:54:53.120 --> 00:54:54.120
is only

00:54:54.120 --> 00:54:55.120
midrabbanan.

00:54:55.120 --> 00:54:56.120
It's telling you

00:54:56.120 --> 00:54:57.120
very clearly.

00:54:57.120 --> 00:54:58.120
But,

00:54:58.120 --> 00:54:59.120
the Hakamin,

00:54:59.120 --> 00:55:00.120
they didn't want to

00:55:00.120 --> 00:55:01.120
politicize this.

00:55:01.120 --> 00:55:02.120
But this is

00:55:02.120 --> 00:55:03.120
an institution

00:55:03.120 --> 00:55:04.120
made by the

00:55:04.120 --> 00:55:05.120
Hakamin.

00:55:05.120 --> 00:55:06.120
But I bring

00:55:06.120 --> 00:55:07.120
this following proof.

00:55:07.120 --> 00:55:08.120
That when

00:55:08.120 --> 00:55:09.120
the rabbis

00:55:09.120 --> 00:55:10.120
redefine

00:55:10.120 --> 00:55:11.120
something

00:55:11.120 --> 00:55:12.120
in the Torah.

00:55:12.120 --> 00:55:13.120
Example.

00:55:13.120 --> 00:55:14.120
The basukh

00:55:14.120 --> 00:55:15.120
says,

00:55:15.120 --> 00:55:16.120
ikah ishasha.

00:55:16.120 --> 00:55:17.120
Come,

00:55:17.120 --> 00:55:18.120
the Hakamin,

00:55:18.120 --> 00:55:19.120
through derasha,

00:55:19.120 --> 00:55:20.120
say,

00:55:20.120 --> 00:55:21.120
ikah bekesef.

00:55:21.120 --> 00:55:22.120
That definition

00:55:22.120 --> 00:55:23.120
becomes

00:55:23.120 --> 00:55:24.120
the orikta

00:55:24.120 --> 00:55:25.120
until another

00:55:25.120 --> 00:55:26.120
beddin

00:55:26.120 --> 00:55:27.120
will

00:55:27.120 --> 00:55:28.120
abrogate it.

00:55:28.120 --> 00:55:29.120
You understand?

00:55:29.120 --> 00:55:30.120
That is the

00:55:30.120 --> 00:55:31.120
point that I

00:55:31.120 --> 00:55:32.120
did.

00:55:32.120 --> 00:55:33.120
For this,

00:55:33.120 --> 00:55:34.120
the best

00:55:34.120 --> 00:55:35.120
and the subject

00:55:35.120 --> 00:55:36.120
is written in

00:55:36.120 --> 00:55:37.120
my

00:55:37.120 --> 00:55:38.120
ayyur-e-murshidur

00:55:38.120 --> 00:55:39.120
al-rambam.

00:55:39.120 --> 00:55:40.120
I explain this

00:55:40.120 --> 00:55:41.120
and I bring

00:55:41.120 --> 00:55:42.120
dozens of

00:55:42.120 --> 00:55:43.120
examples.

00:55:43.120 --> 00:55:44.120
Not only

00:55:44.120 --> 00:55:45.120
on kiddushin.

00:55:45.120 --> 00:55:46.120
I mean,

00:55:46.120 --> 00:55:47.120
I think that,

00:55:47.120 --> 00:55:48.120
alright,

00:55:48.120 --> 00:55:49.120
let me give you

00:55:49.120 --> 00:55:50.120
this example.

00:55:50.120 --> 00:55:51.120
The Torah says,

00:55:51.120 --> 00:55:52.120
but the Torah

00:55:52.120 --> 00:55:53.120
in no place

00:55:53.120 --> 00:55:54.120
says how many

00:55:54.120 --> 00:55:55.120
threads.

00:55:55.120 --> 00:55:56.120
Not

00:55:56.120 --> 00:55:57.120
how many

00:55:57.120 --> 00:55:58.120
threads.

00:55:58.120 --> 00:55:59.120
Four threads,

00:55:59.120 --> 00:56:00.120
seven threads,

00:56:00.120 --> 00:56:01.120
five threads,

00:56:01.120 --> 00:56:02.120
doesn't say.

00:56:02.120 --> 00:56:03.120
Now,

00:56:03.120 --> 00:56:04.120
listen to this.

00:56:04.120 --> 00:56:05.120
Come,

00:56:05.120 --> 00:56:06.120
finally,

00:56:06.120 --> 00:56:07.120
through derashot.

00:56:07.120 --> 00:56:08.120
They say

00:56:08.120 --> 00:56:09.120
four threads

00:56:09.120 --> 00:56:10.120
because they

00:56:10.120 --> 00:56:11.120
wanted to have

00:56:11.120 --> 00:56:12.120
uniformity.

00:56:12.120 --> 00:56:13.120
Today,

00:56:13.120 --> 00:56:14.120
according to

00:56:14.120 --> 00:56:15.120
al-rambam,

00:56:15.120 --> 00:56:16.120
if you would

00:56:16.120 --> 00:56:17.120
wear as a seat

00:56:17.120 --> 00:56:18.120
with three threads

00:56:18.120 --> 00:56:19.120
or with

00:56:19.120 --> 00:56:20.120
five threads,

00:56:20.120 --> 00:56:21.120
you

00:56:21.120 --> 00:56:22.120
didn't

00:56:22.120 --> 00:56:23.120
fulfill the

00:56:23.120 --> 00:56:24.120
misbah

00:56:24.120 --> 00:56:25.120
in the Torah

00:56:25.120 --> 00:56:26.120
and you

00:56:26.120 --> 00:56:27.120
abarta

00:56:27.120 --> 00:56:28.120
mishubal

00:56:28.120 --> 00:56:29.120
tosifu

00:56:29.120 --> 00:56:30.120
al-tigra.

00:56:30.120 --> 00:56:31.120
Why?

00:56:31.120 --> 00:56:32.120
Because

00:56:32.120 --> 00:56:33.120
once,

00:56:33.120 --> 00:56:34.120
now the

00:56:34.120 --> 00:56:35.120
hagamim

00:56:35.120 --> 00:56:36.120
defined it

00:56:36.120 --> 00:56:37.120
four threads.

00:56:37.120 --> 00:56:38.120
That definition

00:56:38.120 --> 00:56:39.120
becomes

00:56:39.120 --> 00:56:40.120
in the Torah.

00:56:40.120 --> 00:56:41.120
Of course,

00:56:41.120 --> 00:56:42.120
if there would

00:56:42.120 --> 00:56:43.120
be another

00:56:43.120 --> 00:56:44.120
betina ghadol,

00:56:44.120 --> 00:56:45.120
they would

00:56:45.120 --> 00:56:46.120
have the

00:56:46.120 --> 00:56:47.120
right to

00:56:47.120 --> 00:56:48.120
redefine it.

00:56:48.120 --> 00:56:49.120
So far,

00:56:49.120 --> 00:56:50.120
they could

00:56:50.120 --> 00:56:51.120
redefine

00:56:51.120 --> 00:56:52.120
and something

00:56:52.120 --> 00:56:53.120
which is

00:56:53.120 --> 00:56:54.120
like

00:56:54.120 --> 00:56:55.120
keikah

00:56:55.120 --> 00:56:56.120
ishishah,

00:56:56.120 --> 00:56:57.120
the hagamim

00:56:57.120 --> 00:56:58.120
they could

00:56:58.120 --> 00:56:59.120
redefine.

00:56:59.120 --> 00:57:00.120
And I show,

00:57:00.120 --> 00:57:01.120
I don't want to

00:57:01.120 --> 00:57:02.120
go into the details

00:57:02.120 --> 00:57:03.120
how the hagamim

00:57:03.120 --> 00:57:04.120
for instance

00:57:04.120 --> 00:57:05.120
say

00:57:05.120 --> 00:57:06.120
sometimes

00:57:06.120 --> 00:57:07.120
the rabbis

00:57:07.120 --> 00:57:08.120
they

00:57:08.120 --> 00:57:09.120
abrogated

00:57:09.120 --> 00:57:10.120
the marriage.

00:57:10.120 --> 00:57:11.120
And I show

00:57:11.120 --> 00:57:12.120
that this is

00:57:12.120 --> 00:57:13.120
only an

00:57:13.120 --> 00:57:14.120
kedushim

00:57:14.120 --> 00:57:15.120
of kesef

00:57:15.120 --> 00:57:16.120
because

00:57:16.120 --> 00:57:17.120
since that

00:57:17.120 --> 00:57:18.120
kesef

00:57:18.120 --> 00:57:19.120
they could

00:57:19.120 --> 00:57:20.120
redefine it

00:57:20.120 --> 00:57:21.120
any way

00:57:21.120 --> 00:57:22.120
they wanted.

00:57:22.120 --> 00:57:23.120
And that's why

00:57:23.120 --> 00:57:24.120
they wanted to

00:57:24.120 --> 00:57:25.120
encourage

00:57:25.120 --> 00:57:26.120
marriage

00:57:26.120 --> 00:57:27.120
through kesef

00:57:27.120 --> 00:57:28.120
so that they

00:57:28.120 --> 00:57:29.120
have the power

00:57:29.120 --> 00:57:30.120
to redefine

00:57:30.120 --> 00:57:31.120
and to

00:57:31.120 --> 00:57:32.120
annul the

00:57:32.120 --> 00:57:33.120
marriage

00:57:33.120 --> 00:57:34.120
if they want

00:57:34.120 --> 00:57:35.120
and so on

00:57:35.120 --> 00:57:36.120
and those

00:57:36.120 --> 00:57:37.120
type of

00:57:37.120 --> 00:57:38.120
things.

00:57:38.120 --> 00:57:39.120
Very interesting.

00:57:39.120 --> 00:57:40.120
So you have

00:57:40.120 --> 00:57:41.120
to

00:57:41.120 --> 00:57:42.120
do this.

00:57:42.120 --> 00:57:43.120
The hagamim

00:57:43.120 --> 00:57:44.120
says

00:57:44.120 --> 00:57:45.120
the kesef

00:57:45.120 --> 00:57:46.120
is not akat.

00:57:46.120 --> 00:57:47.120
The proof

00:57:47.120 --> 00:57:48.120
is the

00:57:48.120 --> 00:57:49.120
kesef.

00:57:49.120 --> 00:57:50.120
So therefore

00:57:50.120 --> 00:57:51.120
they say

00:57:51.120 --> 00:57:52.120
that is the proof

00:57:52.120 --> 00:57:53.120
that this is going

00:57:53.120 --> 00:57:54.120
to be

00:57:54.120 --> 00:57:55.120
in the Torah.

00:57:55.120 --> 00:57:56.120
What?

00:57:56.120 --> 00:57:57.120
No, no, no.

00:57:57.120 --> 00:57:58.120
Yes.

00:57:58.120 --> 00:57:59.120
It's not

00:57:59.120 --> 00:58:00.120
even a custom.

00:58:00.120 --> 00:58:01.120
It's a nice

00:58:01.120 --> 00:58:02.120
habit.

00:58:02.120 --> 00:58:03.120
If you want

00:58:03.120 --> 00:58:04.120
to do it,

00:58:04.120 --> 00:58:05.120
do it.

00:58:05.120 --> 00:58:06.120
Sometimes

00:58:06.120 --> 00:58:07.120
I do it.

00:58:07.120 --> 00:58:08.120
Sometimes

00:58:08.120 --> 00:58:09.120
I don't do it.

00:58:09.120 --> 00:58:10.120
It depends

00:58:10.120 --> 00:58:11.120
if I remember

00:58:11.120 --> 00:58:12.120
or I don't

00:58:12.120 --> 00:58:13.120
remember.

00:58:13.120 --> 00:58:14.120
It's nice.

00:58:14.120 --> 00:58:15.120
I do it

00:58:15.120 --> 00:58:16.120
many times.

00:58:16.120 --> 00:58:17.120
Each

00:58:17.120 --> 00:58:18.120
separately.

00:58:18.120 --> 00:58:19.120
I don't

00:58:19.120 --> 00:58:20.120
do it

00:58:20.120 --> 00:58:21.120
with anyone else.

00:58:21.120 --> 00:58:22.120
I only

00:58:22.120 --> 00:58:23.120
do it

00:58:23.120 --> 00:58:24.120
when I

00:58:24.120 --> 00:58:25.120
remember

00:58:25.120 --> 00:58:26.120
it.

00:58:26.120 --> 00:58:27.120
That's

00:58:27.120 --> 00:58:28.120
it.

00:58:28.120 --> 00:58:29.120
I do

00:58:29.120 --> 00:58:30.120
it.

00:58:30.120 --> 00:58:31.120
I don't

00:58:31.120 --> 00:58:32.120
do it

00:58:32.120 --> 00:58:33.120
with anyone

00:58:33.120 --> 00:58:34.120
else.

00:58:34.120 --> 00:58:35.120
I don't

00:58:35.120 --> 00:58:36.120
even

00:58:36.120 --> 00:58:37.120
do

00:58:37.120 --> 00:58:38.120
it

00:58:38.120 --> 00:58:39.120
with

00:58:39.120 --> 00:58:40.120
my mom.

00:58:40.120 --> 00:58:41.120
I

00:58:41.120 --> 00:58:42.120
don't

00:58:42.120 --> 00:58:43.120
do it

00:58:43.120 --> 00:58:44.120
with

00:58:44.120 --> 00:58:45.120
my mom.

